{
  "title": "6: al-An'aam الأنعام",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَجَعَلَ الظُّلُمٰتِ وَالنُّوْرَ  ؕ ثُمَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِرَبِّهِمْ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(1)\nAALHAMDU LILLAAHE LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA ZOLOMAATE WAALNNOORA SUMMA LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-RABBEHIM YAA’DELOONA.\nPraise be Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth, and made the darkness and the light. Yet those who reject Faith hold (others) as equal, with their Guardian-Lord. \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ ثُمَّ قَضٰۤى اَجَلًا  ؕ وَاَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّى عِنْدَهٗ ثُمَّ اَنْتُمْ تَمْتَرُوْنَ‏(2)\nHOWA LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN TEENIN SUMMA QAZAA AAJALAN WA AJALUM AJALIM I’NDAHU SUMMA ANTUM TAMTAROON.\nHe it is created you from clay, and then decreed a stated term (for you). And there is in His presence another determined term; yet ye doubt within yourselves! \nوَهُوَ اللّٰهُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَفِى الْاَرْضِؕ يَعْلَمُ سِرَّكُمْ وَ جَهْرَكُمْ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(3)\nWA HOWA LAAHO FIL SAMAAWAATE WA ARZ YA’LAMO SERRAKUM WA JAHRAKUM YA’LAMO MAA TAKSEBOONA.\nAnd He is Allah in the heavens and on earth. He knoweth what ye hide, and what ye reveal, and He knoweth the (recompense) which ye earn (by your deeds). \nوَمَا تَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ اٰيَةٍ مِّنْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ اِلَّا كَانُوْا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِيْنَ‏(4)\nWA MAA TAA-TEEHIM MIN AAYATIM MIN AAYAATIL RABBEHIM ILLAA KAANOO A’NHAA MOA’REZEEN.\nBut never did a single one of the signs of their Lord reach them, but they turned away therefrom. \nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْؕ فَسَوْفَ يَاْتِيْهِمْ اَنْۢبٰٓؤُا مَا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(5)\nFAQAD KAZZABOO BIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAAHUM FA-SAWFA YAATEEHIM AANBAAAUA MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd now they reject the truth when it reaches them: but soon shall they learn the reality of what they used to mock at. \nاَلَمْ يَرَوْا كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ مَّكَّنّٰهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مَا لَمْ نُمَكِّنْ لَّكُمْ وَاَرْسَلْنَا السَّمَآءَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّدْرَارًا وَّجَعَلْنَا الْاَنْهٰرَ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهِمْ فَاَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ وَاَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قَرْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‏(6)\nALAM YARAW KAM AHLAKNAL MIN QABLEHIM MIN QARNIN MMAKKANNAAHUM FIL ARZE MAA LAM LAHUM LAKUM WA ARSALNAA SAMAAA-AD A’LAYHIM MMEDRAARAN WA JA-A’LNAA AL-AANHAARA TAJREE MIN TAHTEHEM FA AHLAKNAAHUM BEZUNOOBEHEM WA ANSHAANAA MIN BA’DEHIM QARNAN AAKHEREEN.\nSee they not how many of those before them We did destroy? generations We had established on the earth, in strength such as We have not given to you - for whom We poured out rain from the skies in abundance, and gave (fertile) streams flowing beneath their (feet): yet for their sins We destroyed them, and raised in their wake fresh generations (to succeed them). \nوَلَوْ نَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكَ كِتٰبًا فِىْ قِرْطَاسٍ فَلَمَسُوْهُ بِاَيْدِيْهِمْ لَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(7)\nWA LAW NAZZALNAA A’LAYKA KETAABAA FEE QERTAASIN FALAMASOOHU BE-AYDEEHIM LAQAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nIf We had sent unto thee a written (message) on parchment, so that they could touch it with their hands, the Unbelievers would have been sure to say: “This is nothing but obvious magic!” \nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ مَلَكٌ ؕ وَلَوْ اَنْزَلْنَا مَلَكًا لَّقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ ثُمَّ لَا يُنْظَرُوْنَ‏(8)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE MALAKUN WA LAW ANZALNAA MALAKAN LLAQUZEAAA MIN SUMMA LAA HUM YUNZAROON.\nThey say: “Why is not an angel sent down to him?” If we did send down an angel, the matter would be settled at once, and no respite would be granted them. \nوَلَوْ جَعَلْنٰهُ مَلَكًا لَّجَعَلْنٰهُ رَجُلًا وَّلَلَبَسْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّا يَلْبِسُوْنَ‏(9)\nWA LAW LAW MALAKAN LLAJAA’ALNAAHU RAJULAN WWALALABASNAA A’LAYHIM MAA YALBESOONA.\nIf We had made it an angel, We should have sent him as a man, and We should certainly have caused them confusion in a matter which they have already covered with confusion. \nوَلَقَدِ اسْتُهْزِئَ بِرُسُلٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَحَاقَ بِالَّذِيْنَ سَخِرُوْا مِنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(10)\nLAQADIS ASTUHZEA BERUSULIN MIN QABLEKA FAHAAQA BE-LAZEENA SAKHEROOA MINHUM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nMocked were (many) messengers before thee; but their scoffers were hemmed in by the thing that they mocked. \nقُلْ سِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ ثُمَّ انْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(11)\nQUL SEEROO FIL ARZE SUMMA ANZUROOA KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MOKAZZEBEENAZ.\nSay: “Travel through the earth and see what was the end of those who rejected Truth.” \nقُلْ لِّمَنْ مَّا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ قُلْ لِّلّٰهِؕ كَتَبَ عَلٰى نَفْسِهِ الرَّحْمَةَ  ؕ لَيَجْمَعَنَّكُمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ ؕ اَلَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(12)\nQUL LEMAN MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ QUL LELLAAHE KATABAL A’LAA NAFSEHE AR-RAHMATA LAYAJMAA’ANNAKUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAA RAYBA FEEHE LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM FAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nSay: “To whom belongeth all that is in the heavens and on earth?” Say: “To Allah. He hath inscribed for Himself (the rule of) Mercy. That He will gather you together for the Day of Judgment, there is no doubt whatever. It is they who have lost their own souls, that will not believe. \nوَلَهٗ مَا سَكَنَ فِى الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِؕ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(13)\nWA LAHU MAA SAKANA FIL LAYLE WA WA WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\n To him belongeth all that dwelleth (or lurketh) in the night and the day. For he is the one who heareth and knoweth all things.” \nقُلْ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَتَّخِذُ وَلِيًّا فَاطِرِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَهُوَ يُطْعِمُ وَلَا يُطْعَمُؕ قُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ اَوَّلَ مَنْ اَسْلَمَ وَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(14)\nQUL AAGHAYRA LAAHE AATTAKHEZU WALIYYANW FAATERE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA HOWA YUTE’EMU WA LAA YUTA’AMU QUL INNEE AN A-A’BODA AN SHAY-IWN WA AWWALA MAN ASLAMA WA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSay: “Shall I take for my protector any other than Allah, the Maker of the heavens and the earth? And He it is that feedeth but is not fed.” Say: “Nay! but I am commanded to be the first of those who bow to Allah (in Islam), and be not thou of the company of those who join gods with Allah.” \nقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اِنْ عَصَيْتُ رَبِّىْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(15)\nQUL INNEE AKHAAFO IN A’ASAYTU RABBEE A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nSay: “I would, if I disobeyed my Lord, indeed have fear of the penalty of a Mighty Day. \nمَنْ يُّصْرَفْ عَنْهُ يَوْمَئِذٍ فَقَدْ رَحِمَهٗؕ وَ ذٰ لِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(16)\nMAN YYUSRAF A’NHO YAWMA-EZIN FAQAD RAHEMAH WA ZAA LEKA FAWZUL MOBEEN.\n“On that day, if the penalty is averted from any, it is due to Allah's mercy; And that would be (Salvation), the obvious fulfilment of all desire. \nوَاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكَ اللّٰهُ بِضُرٍّ فَلَا كَاشِفَ لَهٗۤ اِلَّا هُوَؕ وَاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكَ بِخَيْرٍ فَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(17)\nWA YYAMSASKA LAAHO BEZURRIN FALAA KAASHEFA LAHU ILLAA HOO WA YYAMSASKA BE-KHAYRIN FAHOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\n“If Allah touch thee with affliction, none can remove it but He; if He touch thee with happiness, He hath power over all things. \nوَهُوَ الْقَاهِرُ فَوْقَ عِبَادِهٖ ؕ وَهُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(18)\nWA HOWA AL-QAAHERU FAWQA E’BAADEHI WA HOWA HAKEEM KHABEER.\n“He is the irresistible, (watching) from above over His worshippers; and He is the Wise, acquainted with all things.” \nقُلْ اَىُّ شَىْءٍ اَكْبَرُ شَهَادَةً ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ ۙ شَهِيْدٌ ۢ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْ وَاُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنُ لِاُنْذِرَكُمْ بِهٖ وَمَنْۢ بَلَغَ ؕ اَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَشْهَدُوْنَ اَنَّ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اٰلِهَةً اُخْرٰىؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَشْهَدُ ۚ قُلْ اِنَّمَا هُوَ اِلٰهٌ وَّاحِدٌ وَّاِنَّنِىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَۘ‏(19)\nQUL AAA SHAY-IN AKBARO SHA-HAADATAN QOLIL LAAHO WA BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM WA OOHEYA ELAYYA HAAZAA QUR-AANO LEAUNZERAKUM BEHI WA MAN BALAGHA A-INNAKUM LATASHHADOONA ANNAL LAAHA LAAHE AALEHATAL AUKHRAA QUL LAA AASHHADU QUL INNAMAA HOWA ELAAHUN WAAHED WWAANNANEAA BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUSHREKOONA.\nSay: “What thing is most weighty in evidence?” Say: “Allah is witness between me and you; This Qur'an hath been revealed to me by inspiration, that I may warn you and all whom it reaches. Can ye possibly bear witness that besides Allah there is another Allah?” Say: “Nay! I cannot bear witness!” Say: “But in truth He is the one Allah, and I truly am innocent of (your blasphemy of) joining others with Him.” \nاَ لَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَعْرِفُوْنَهٗ كَمَا يَعْرِفُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَهُمُۘ اَ لَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(20)\nA’ZAABAN LLAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YA’REFOONAHU KAMAA YA’REFOONA AABNAAAHUMU A’ZAABAN LLAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM FAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThose to whom We have given the Book know this as they know their own sons. Those who have lost their own souls refuse therefore to believe. \nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW KAZZABA BEAAAYAATEH INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nWho doth more wrong than he who inventeth a lie against Allah or rejecteth His signs? But verily the wrong-doers never shall prosper. \nوَيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ نَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْۤا اَيْنَ شُرَكَآؤُكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA YAWMA NAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A SUMMA NAQOOLU LILLAZEENA ASHRAKOO AYNA SHURAKAAUKUMU LAZEENA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\nOne day shall We gather them all together: We shall say to those who ascribed partners (to Us): “Where are the partners whom ye (invented and) talked about?” \nثُمَّ لَمْ تَكُنْ فِتْنَتُهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْا وَاللّٰهِ رَبِّنَا مَا كُنَّا مُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(23)\nSUMMA LAM TAKUN FETNATUHUM ILLAA AN QAALOO WA LAAHE RABBENAA MAA KUNNAA MUSHREKEENA.\nThere will then be (left) no subterfuge for them but to say: “By Allah our Lord, we were not those who joined gods with Allah.” \nاُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَذَبُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(24)\nAUNZUR KAYFA KAZABOOA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nBehold! how they lie against their own souls! But the (lie) which they invented will leave them in the lurch. \nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّسْتَمِعُ اِلَيْكَ ۚ وَجَعَلْنَا عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ اَكِنَّةً اَنْ يَّفْقَهُوْهُ وَفِىْۤ اٰذَانِهِمْ وَقْرًا ؕ وَاِنْ يَّرَوْا كُلَّ اٰيَةٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْا بِهَا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا جَآءُوْكَ يُجَادِلُوْنَكَ يَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(25)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYASTAMEU’U ELAYKA WA JA-A’LNAA A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM AAKENNATAN AN YYAFQAHOOHU WA FEE AAZAANEHIM WAQRAN WA YYARAWA KULLA AAYATIM LAA YOAMENOO BEHAA HATTAA EZAA JAAOOKA YUJAADELOONAKA YAQOOLO LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nOf them there are some who (pretend to) listen to thee; but We have thrown veils on their hearts, So they understand it not, and deafness in their ears; if they saw every one of the signs, not they will believe in them; in so much that when they come to thee, they (but) dispute with thee; the Unbelievers say: “These are nothing but tales of the ancients.” \nوَهُمْ يَنْهَوْنَ عَنْهُ وَيَنْئَوْنَ عَنْهُۚ وَاِنْ يُّهْلِكُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(26)\nWA HUM YANHAWNA A’NHO WAYANAWNA A’NHO WA YYUHLEKOONA ILLAA ANFOSAHUM WA MAA YASH-O’ROON.\nOthers they keep away from it, and themselves they keep away; but they only destroy their own souls, and they perceive it not. \nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ وُقِفُوْا عَلَى النَّارِ فَقَالُوْا يٰلَيْتَنَا نُرَدُّ وَلَا نُكَذِّبَ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّنَا وَنَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(27)\nWA LAW TARAAA IZ WUQEFOOA A’LAL NAAR FA-QAALOO YAALAYTANAA NURADDU WA LAA NUKAZZEBA BE-AAYAATIL RABBENAA WA NAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nIf thou couldst but see when they are confronted with the Fire! They will say: “Would that we were but sent back! Then would we not reject the signs of our Lord, but would be amongst those who believe!” \nبَلْ بَدَا لَهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُخْفُوْنَ مِنْ قَبْلُؕ وَلَوْ رُدُّوْا لَعَادُوْا لِمَا نُهُوْا عَنْهُ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(28)\nBAL BADAA LAHUM MAA KAANOO YUKHFOONA MIN QABL WA WA LAW RUDDOOA LAA’AADOOA LEMAKH NUHOOA A’NHO WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nYea, in their own (eyes) will become manifest what before they concealed. But if they were returned, they would certainly relapse to the things they were forbidden, for they are indeed liars. \nوَقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَبْعُوْثِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA QAALOO IN HEYA ILLAA HAYAATUNAA DUNYAA WA MAA NAHNO BEMABU’OOSEENA.\nAnd they (sometimes) say: “There is nothing except our life on this earth, and never shall we be raised up again.” \nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ وُقِفُوْا عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ ؕ قَالَ اَلَيْسَ هٰذَا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى وَرَبِّنَا ؕ قَالَ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(30)\nWA LAW TARAAA IZ WUQEFOOA A’LAA RABBEHIM QAALA A-LAYSA HAAZAA BIL-HAQQE QAALOO BALAA WARABBENAA QAALA FAZOOQOOA A’ZAABA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKFOROONA.\nIf thou couldst but see when they are confronted with their Lord! He will say: “Is not this the truth?” They will say: “Yea, by our Lord!” He will say: “Taste ye then the penalty, because ye rejected Faith.” \nقَدْ خَسِرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِلِقَآءِ اللّٰهِؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَتْهُمُ السَّاعَةُ بَغْتَةً قَالُوْا يٰحَسْرَتَنَا عَلٰى مَا فَرَّطْنَا فِيْهَا ۙ وَهُمْ يَحْمِلُوْنَ اَوْزَارَهُمْ عَلٰى ظُهُوْرِهِمْؕ اَلَا سَآءَ مَا يَزِرُوْنَ‏(31)\nQAD KHASERA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BELEQAAE LAAH HATTAA EZAA JAAA-ATHOMUL SAA-A’TO BAGHTATANW QAALOO YAAHASRATANAA A’LAA MAA FARRATNAA FEEHAA WA HUM YAHMELOONA AAWZAARAHUM A’LAA ZUHOOREHEM ALAA SAAA-A MAA YAZEROONA.\nLost indeed are they who treat it as a falsehood that they must meet Allah, until on a sudden the hour is on them, and they say: “Ah! woe unto us that we took no thought of it”; for they bear their burdens on their backs, and evil indeed are the burdens that they bear? \nوَ مَا الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَاۤ اِلَّا لَعِبٌ وَّلَهْوٌ ؕ وَلَلدَّارُ الْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(32)\nWA MAA HAYAATUD DUNYAA ILLAA LAE’EBUN WWALAHWUN WALALDDAARU AAKHERATO KHAYRUL LIL-LAZEENA YATTAQOONA AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nWhat is the life of this world but play and amusement? But best is the home in the hereafter, for those who are righteous. Will ye not then understand? \nقَدْ نَعْلَمُ اِنَّهٗ لَيَحْزُنُكَ الَّذِىْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ فَاِنَّهُمْ لَا يُكَذِّبُوْنَكَ وَلٰكِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(33)\nQAD NA’LAMO INNAHU LAYAHZUNUKA LAZEE YAQOOLOONA FA INNAHUM LAA YUKAZZEBOONAKA LAAKINNAL ZAALEMEEN BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE YAJHADOON.\nWe know indeed the grief which their words do cause thee: It is not thee they reject: it is the signs of Allah, which the wicked contemn. \nوَلَقَدْ كُذِّبَتْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَصَبَرُوْا عَلٰى مَا كُذِّبُوْا وَاُوْذُوْا حَتّٰٓى اَتٰٮهُمْ نَصْرُنَا ۚ وَلَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمٰتِ اللّٰهِ ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَكَ مِنْ نَّبَاِى الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(34)\nWA LAQAD KUZZEBAT RUSULUN MIN QABLEKA FA SABAROO A’LAA MAA KUZZEBOOA WAAWZOOA HATTAA ATAAHUM NASRUNAA WA LAA MUBADDELA LEKALEMAATE LAAHE WA LAQAD JAAA-AKA MIN NNABAAAA MURSALEEN.\nRejected were the messengers before thee: with patience and constancy they bore their rejection and their wrongs, until Our aid did reach them: there is none that can alter the words (and decrees) of Allah. Already hast thou received some account of those messengers. \nوَاِنْ كَانَ كَبُرَ عَلَيْكَ اِعْرَاضُهُمْ فَاِنِ اسْتَطَعْتَ اَنْ تَبْتَغِىَ نَفَقًا فِى الْاَرْضِ اَوْ سُلَّمًا فِى السَّمَآءِ فَتَاْتِيَهُمْ بِاٰيَةٍ ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَجَمَعَهُمْ عَلَى الْهُدٰى فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(35)\nWA KAANA KABURA A’LAYKA AEA’RAAZUHUM FA-ENIN ASTATAA’TA AN TABTAGHEAAA NAFAQAN FIL ARZE AW SULLAMAN FIL SAMAAA-E FATAATEEHUM BE-AAYATIL WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LAJAMAA’AHUM A’LAL HODAA FALAA TAKOONANNA MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nIf their spurning is hard on thy mind, yet if thou wert able to seek a tunnel in the ground or a ladder to the skies and bring them a sign, (what good?). If it were Allah's will, He could gather them together unto true guidance: so be not thou amongst those who are swayed by ignorance (and impatience)! \nاِنَّمَا يَسْتَجِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْمَعُوْنَ ؕؔ وَالْمَوْتٰى يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ ثُمَّ اِلَيْهِ يُرْجَعُوْنَؔ‏(36)\nINNAMAA YASTAJEEBU LAZEENA YAS-MA-O’ONA WA MAWTAA YABA’ASUHUMU LAAHO SUMMA ELAYHE YURJAU’OONA.\n Those who listen (in truth), be sure, will accept: as to the dead, Allah will raise them up; then will they be turned unto Him. \nوَ قَالُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ قُلْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَادِرٌ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يُّنَزِّلَ اٰيَةً وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA NUZZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEH QUL INNAL LAAHA QAADERUN A’LAA AN YONAZZELAL AAYATAL WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThey say: “Why is not a sign sent down to him from his Lord?” Say: “Allah hath certainly power to send down a sign: but most of them understand not. \nوَمَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا طٰۤئِرٍ يَّطِيْرُ بِجَنَاحَيْهِ اِلَّاۤ اُمَمٌ اَمْثَالُكُمْؕ مَا فَرَّطْنَا فِى الْكِتٰبِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(38)\nWA MAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL FIL ARZE WA LAA TAAERIN YYATEERU BEJANAAHAYHE ILLAA OMAMUM AAMSAALUKUM MAA FARRATNAA FIL KETAABE MIN SHAY-IN SUMMA ELAA RABBEHIM YUHSHAROONA.\nThere is not an animal (that lives) on the earth, nor a being that flies on its wings, but (forms part of) communities like you. Nothing have we omitted from the Book, and they (all) shall be gathered to their Lord in the end. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا صُمٌّ وَّبُكْمٌ فِى الظُّلُمٰتِؕ مَنْ يَّشَاِ اللّٰهُ يُضْلِلْهُ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّشَاْ يَجْعَلْهُ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(39)\nWAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA SUMMUM WWABUKMUN FIL ZOLOMAAT MAN YYASHAA LAAHO YUZLELHU WA MAN YYASHAA YAJA’ALHU A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nThose who reject our signs are deaf and dumb, in the midst of darkness profound: whom Allah willeth, He leaveth to wander: whom He willeth, He placeth on the way that is straight. \nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتَكُمْ اِنْ اَتٰٮكُمْ عَذَابُ اللّٰهِ اَوْ اَ تَتْكُمُ السَّاعَةُ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ تَدْعُوْنَۚ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(40)\nQUL AARAAYTAKUM IN AATAAKUM A’ZAABO LAAHE AW A’ZAABAN TATKUMU SAA-A’TO AAGHAYRA LAAHE TADU’OONA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nSay: “Think ye to yourselves, if there come upon you the wrath of Allah, or the Hour (that ye dread), would ye then call upon other than Allah? (reply) if ye are truthful! \nبَلْ اِيَّاهُ تَدْعُوْنَ فَيَكْشِفُ مَا تَدْعُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ اِنْ شَآءَ وَتَنْسَوْنَ مَا تُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(41)\nBAL IYYAAHO TADU’OONA FAYAKSHEFU MAA TADU’OONA ELAYHE IN SHAAA-AL WA TANSAWNA MAA TUSHREKOONA.\n“Nay, On Him would ye call, and if it be His will, He would remove (the distress) which occasioned your call upon Him, and ye would forget (the false gods) which ye join with Him!” \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمَمٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِكَ فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِالْبَاْسَآءِ وَالضَّرَّآءِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَضَرَّعُوْنَ‏(42)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ELAA OMAMIN MIN QABLEKA FAAKHAZNAAHUM BE-BAA-SAAA-E WAZ ZARRAAA-E LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZARRAU’OONA.\nBefore thee We sent (messengers) to many nations, and We afflicted the nations with suffering and adversity, that they might learn humility. \nفَلَوْلَاۤ اِذْ جَآءَهُمْ بَاْسُنَا تَضَرَّعُوْا وَلٰكِنْ قَسَتْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(43)\nFA-LAWLAA IZ JAAA-AHUM BAASUNAA TAZARRAU’OOA WA LAAKIL QASAT QULOOBUHUM WA ZAYYANA LAHOMUL SHAYTAANO MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nWhen the suffering reached them from us, why then did they not learn humility? On the contrary their hearts became hardened, and Satan made their (sinful) acts seem alluring to them. \nفَلَمَّا نَسُوْا مَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖ فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ اَبْوَابَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا فَرِحُوْا بِمَاۤ اُوْتُوْۤا اَخَذْنٰهُمْ بَغْتَةً فَاِذَا هُمْ مُّبْلِسُوْنَ‏(44)\nFALAMMAA NASOOA MAA ZUKKEROOA BEHI FATAHNA A’LAYHIM AABWAABA KULLE SHAY-IN HATTAA EZAA FAREHOO BEMAA OOTOO AAKHAZNAAHUM BAGHTATANW FA-EZAA HUM MMUBLESOONA.\nBut when they forgot the warning they had received, We opened to them the gates of all (good) things, until, in the midst of their enjoyment of Our gifts, on a sudden, We called them to account, when lo! they were plunged in despair! \nفَقُطِعَ دَابِرُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ؕ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(45)\nFAQUTEA’A DAABERU QAWMIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO WA HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nOf the wrong-doers the last remnant was cut off. Praise be to Allah, the Cherisher of the worlds. \nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ اَخَذَ اللّٰهُ سَمْعَكُمْ وَ اَبْصَارَكُمْ وَخَتَمَ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِكُمْ مَّنْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِ يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِهؕ اُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ ثُمَّ هُمْ يَصْدِفُوْنَ‏(46)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN AAKHAZA LAAHO SAMA’AKUM WA AABSAARAKUM WA KHATAMAL A’LAA QOLOOBEKUM MAN ELAAHUN GHAYRO LAAHE YAATEEKUM BEH AUNZUR KAYFA NUSARREFU AAYAATE SUMMA HUM YASDEFOONA.\nSay: “Think ye, if Allah took away your hearing and your sight, and sealed up your hearts, who - a god other than Allah - could restore them to you?” See how We explain the signs by various (symbols); yet they turn aside. \nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتَكُمْ اِنْ اَتٰٮكُمْ عَذَابُ اللّٰهِ بَغْتَةً اَوْ جَهْرَةً هَلْ يُهْلَكُ اِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(47)\nQUL AARAAYTAKUM IN AATAAKUM A’ZAABO LAAHE BAGHTATANW AW JAHRATN HAL YUHLAKU ILLAA AL-QAWMU ZAALEMOON.\nSay: “Think ye, if the punishment of Allah comes to you, whether suddenly or openly, will any be destroyed except those who do wrong? \nوَمَا نُرْسِلُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ اِلَّا مُبَشِّرِيْنَ وَمُنْذِرِيْنَۚ فَمَنْ اٰمَنَ وَاَصْلَحَ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA MAA NURSELU MURSALEEN ILLAA MOBASH-SHEREENA WA MUNZEREEN FAMAN AAMANA WAASLAHA FALAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nWe send the messengers only to give good news and to warn: so those who believe and mend (their lives), upon them shall be no fear, nor shall they grieve. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَمَسُّهُمُ الْعَذَابُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(49)\nWAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA YAMASSUHUMU A’ZAABO BEMAA KAANOO YAFSOQOON.\nBut those who reject our signs, them shall punishment touch, for that they ceased not from transgressing. \nقُلْ لَّاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْ عِنْدِىْ خَزَآئِنُ اللّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اَعْلَمُ الْغَيْبَ وَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْ اِنِّىْ مَلَكٌ ۚ اِنْ اَتَّبِعُ اِلَّا مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَىَّ ؕ قُلْ هَلْ يَسْتَوِى الْاَعْمٰى وَالْبَصِيْرُ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(50)\nQUL LAA AAQOOLU LAKUM E’ENDEAA KHAZAAENUS LAAHE WA LAA A-A’LAMO GHAYBA WA LAA AAQOOLU LAKUM INNEE MALAKUN IN AATTABEU’U ILLAA MAA YOOHAA ELAYYA QUL HAL YASTAWEAA A-A’MAA WAL BASEERU AFALAA TATAFAKKAROONA.\nSay: “I tell you not that with me are the treasures of Allah, nor do I know what is hidden, nor do I tell you I am an angel. I but follow what is revealed to me.” Say: “can the blind be held equal to the seeing?” Will ye then consider not? \nوَاَنْذِرْ بِهِ الَّذِيْنَ يَخَافُوْنَ اَنْ يُّحْشَرُوْۤا اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ وَلِىٌّ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٌ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(51)\nWAANZER BEHIL LAZEENA YAKHAAFOONA AN YYUHSHAROOA ELAA RABBEHIM LAYSA LAHUM MIN DOONEHI WALIYYUN WA LAA SHAFEEA’UN LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\nGive this warning to those in whose (hearts) is the fear that they will be brought (to judgment) before their Lord: except for Him they will have no protector nor intercessor: that they may guard (against evil). \nوَلَا تَطْرُدِ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ بِالْغَدٰوةِ وَالْعَشِىِّ يُرِيْدُوْنَ وَجْهَهٗ ؕ مَا عَلَيْكَ مِنْ حِسَابِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ وَّمَا مِنْ حِسَابِكَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَتَطْرُدَهُمْ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(52)\nWA LAA TATRUDE LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA RABBAHUM BIL-GHADAAWTE WAL A’ASHEAAAE YOREEDOONA WAJHAHU MAA A’LAYKA MIN HESAABEHEM MIN SHAY-IN WA MAA MIN HESAABEKA A’LAYHIM MIN SHAY-IN FATATRUDAHUM FA TAKOONA MENAL ZAALEMEEN.\nSend not away those who call on their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face. In naught art thou accountable for them, and in naught are they accountable for thee, that thou shouldst turn them away, and thus be (one) of the unjust. \nوَكَذٰلِكَ فَتَنَّا بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لِّيَقُوْلُوْۤا اَهٰٓؤُلَآءِ مَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْۢ بَيْنِنَا ؕ اَلَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِاَعْلَمَ بِالشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(53)\nWA KAZAALEKA FATANNAL BA’ZAHUM BE-BA’Z LLEEQOOLOOA AAHAAAULAAE MANNA LAAHO A’LAYHIM MIN BAYNENAA A-LAYSA LAAHO BE-A’ALAMA BEALSSHAAKEREENA.\nThus did We try some of them by comparison with others, that they should say: “Is it these then that Allah hath favoured from amongst us?” Doth not Allah know best those who are grateful? \nوَاِذَا جَآءَكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَقُلْ سَلَمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ كَتَبَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلٰى نَفْسِهِ الرَّحْمَةَ ۙ اَنَّهٗ مَنْ عَمِلَ مِنْكُمْ سُوْٓءًۢا بِجَهَالَةٍ ثُمَّ تَابَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ وَاَصْلَحَۙ فَاَنَّهٗ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(54)\nWA EZAA JAAA-AKA LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BE-AAYAATENAA FAQUL SALAMUN A’LAYKUM KATABAL RABBOKUM A’LAA NAFSEHE AR-RAHMATA ANNAHU MAN A’MELA MINKUM SOOO-AN BEJAHAALATIN SUMMA TAABA MIN BA’DEHI WAASLAHA FA ANNAHU GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nWhen those come to thee who believe in Our signs, Say: “Peace be on you: Your Lord hath inscribed for Himself (the rule of) mercy: verily, if any of you did evil in ignorance, and thereafter repented, and amend (his conduct), lo! He is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ وَلِتَسْتَبِيْنَ سَبِيْلُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(55)\nWA KAZAALEKA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE WALETASTABEENA SABEELU MUJREMEEN.\nThus do We explain the signs in detail: that the way of the sinners may be shown up. \nقُلْ اِنِّىْ نُهِيْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَ تَّبِعُ اَهْوَآءَكُمْۙ قَدْ ضَلَلْتُ اِذًا وَّمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(56)\nQUL INNEE NUHEETU AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAH QUL LAA A’ZAABAN TTABEU’U AAHWAAAKUM QAD ZALALTU EZAL WA MAA ANAA MENAL AL-MUHTADEENA.\nSay: “I am forbidden to worship those - others than Allah - whom ye call upon.” Say: “I will not follow your wain desires: If I did, I would stray from the path, and be not of the company of those who receive guidance.” \nقُلْ اِنِّىْ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَكَذَّبْتُمْ بِهٖؕ مَا عِنْدِىْ مَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ بِهٖؕ اِنِ الْحُكْمُ اِلَّا لِلّٰهِؕ يَقُصُّ الْحَقَّ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْفٰصِلِيْنَ‏(57)\nQUL INNEE A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WA KAZZABTUM BEH MAA E’ENDEAA MAA TAS-TA’JELOONA BEH ENIS HUKMO ILLAA LIL-LAAH YAQUSSO HAQQA WA HOWA KHAYRUR AL-FAASELEENA.\nSay: “For me, I (work) on a clear sign from my Lord, but ye reject Him. What ye would see hastened, is not in my power. The command rests with none but Allah: He declares the truth, and He is the best of judges.” \nقُلْ لَّوْ اَنَّ عِنْدِىْ مَا تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ بِهٖ لَقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْؕ وَاللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِالظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(58)\nQUL LAW ANNAL E’ENDEAA MAA TAS-TA’JELOONA BEHI LAQOZEYA MIN BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM WAL LAAHO A-A’LAMO BIZ-ZAALEMEEN.\nSay: “If what ye would see hastened were in my power, the matter would be settled at once between you and me. But Allah knoweth best those who do wrong.” \nوَعِنْدَهٗ مَفَاتِحُ الْغَيْبِ لَا يَعْلَمُهَاۤ اِلَّا هُوَؕ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا فِى الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِؕ وَمَا تَسْقُطُ مِنْ وَّرَقَةٍ اِلَّا يَعْلَمُهَا وَلَا حَبَّةٍ فِىْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْاَرْضِ وَلَا رَطْبٍ وَّلَا يَابِسٍ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(59)\nWA I’NDAHU MAFAATEHUL GHAYBE LAA YA’LAMOHAA ILLAA HOO, WA YA’LAMO MAA FIL BARRE WAL BAHR, WA MAA TASQOTO MINW WARAQATIN ILLAA YA’LAMOHAA WA LAA HABBATIN FEE ZOLOMAATIL ARZE WA LAA RATBINW WA LAA YAABESIN ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nWith Him are the keys of the unseen, the treasures that none knoweth but He. He knoweth whatever there is on the earth and in the sea. Not a leaf doth fall but with His knowledge: there is not a grain in the darkness (or depths) of the earth, nor anything fresh or dry (green or withered), but is (inscribed) in a record clear (to those who can read). \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ بِالَّيْلِ وَ يَعْلَمُ مَا جَرَحْتُمْ بِالنَّهَارِ ثُمَّ يَبْعَثُكُمْ فِيْهِ لِيُقْضٰٓى اَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّىۚ ثُمَّ اِلَيْهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YATAWAFFAAKUM BIL-LAYLE WA YA’LAMO MAA JARAHTUM BEALNNAHAARE SUMMA YABA’ASUKUM FEEHE LEEQZAAA AJALUM AJALIM SUMMA ELAYHE MARJE-O’KUM SUMMA YUNABBEUKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nIt is He who doth take your souls by night, and hath knowledge of all that ye have done by day: by day doth He raise you up again; that a term appointed be fulfilled; In the end unto Him will be your return; then will He show you the truth of all that ye did. \nوَهُوَ الْقَاهِرُ فَوْقَ عِبَادِهٖ وَيُرْسِلُ عَلَيْكُمْ حَفَظَةً ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَ اَحَدَكُمُ الْمَوْتُ تَوَفَّتْهُ رُسُلُنَا وَهُمْ لَا يُفَرِّطُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA HOWA AL-QAAHERU FAWQA E’BAADEHI WA YURSELUR A’LAYKUM HAFAZATAN HATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AHADAKOMUL MAWTO TAWAFFATHU ROSOLONAA WA HUM LAA YUFARRETOONA.\nHe is the irresistible, (watching) from above over His worshippers, and He sets guardians over you. At length, when death approaches one of you, Our angels take his soul, and they never fail in their duty. \nثُمَّ رُدُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَوْلٰٮهُمُ الْحَقِّؕ اَلَا لَهُ الْحُكْمُ وَهُوَ اَسْرَعُ الْحَاسِبِيْنَ‏(62)\nSUMMA RUDDOOA ELAL LAAHE MAWLAAHUMU HAQQ ALAA LAHUL HUKMO WA HOWA AASRAU’U AL-HAASEBEENA.\nThen are men returned unto Allah, their protector, the (only) reality: Is not His the command? and He is the swiftest in taking account. \nقُلْ مَنْ يُّنَجِّيْكُمْ مِّنْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ تَدْعُوْنَهٗ تَضَرُّعًا وَّخُفْيَةًۚ لَئِنْ اَنْجٰٮنَا مِنْ هٰذِهٖ لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(63)\nQUL MAN YYUNAJJEEKUM MIN ZOLOMAATIL BARRE WAL BAHRE TADU’OONAH TAZARRUA’AN WWAKHUFYATAN LAIL AANJAANAA MIN HAAZEHI LANAKOONANNA MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nSay: “Who is it that delivereth you from the dark recesses of land and sea, when ye call upon Him in humility and silent terror: 'If He only delivers us from these (dangers), (we vow) we shall truly show our gratitude'?” \nقُلِ اللّٰهُ يُنَجِّيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا وَمِنْ كُلِّ كَرْبٍ ثُمَّ اَنْتُمْ تُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(64)\nQOLIL LAAHO YUNAJJEEKUM MINHAA WA MIN KULLE KARBIN SUMMA ANTUM TUSHREKOONA.\nSay “It is Allah that delivereth you from these and all (other) distresses: and yet ye worship false gods!” \nقُلْ هُوَ الْقَادِرُ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّبْعَثَ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابًا مِّنْ فَوْقِكُمْ اَوْ مِنْ تَحْتِ اَرْجُلِكُمْ اَوْ يَلْبِسَكُمْ شِيَعًا وَّيُذِيْقَ بَعْضَكُمْ بَاْسَ بَعْضٍؕ اُنْظُرْ كَيْفَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَفْقَهُوْنَ‏(65)\nQUL HOWA AL-QAADERU A’LAA AN YYABA’ASA A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAN MIN FAWQEKUM AW MIN TAHTE AARJULEKUM AW YALBESAKUM AHLAHAA WWAYUZEEQA BAA’ZAKUM BAASA BA’Z WA AUNZUR KAYFA NUSARREFU AAYAATE LA-A’LLAHUM YAFQAHOON.\nSay: “He hath power to send calamities on you, from above and below, or to cover you with confusion in party strife, giving you a taste of mutual vengeance - each from the other.” See how We explain the signs by various (symbols); that they may understand. \nوَكَذَّبَ بِهٖ قَوْمُكَ وَهُوَ الْحَقُّ ؕ قُلْ لَّسْتُ عَلَيْكُمْ بِوَكِيْلٍؕ‏(66)\nWA KAZZABA BEHI QAWMUKA WA HOWA HAQQO QUL LLASTU A’LAYKUM BEWAKEELIN.\nBut thy people reject this, though it is the truth. Say: “Not mine is the responsibility for arranging your affairs; \nلِّكُلِّ نَبَاٍ مُّسْتَقَرٌّ وَّسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(67)\nLEKULLE NABAA MMUSTAQARRUN WWASAWFA TA’LAMOON.\nFor every message is a limit of time, and soon shall ye know it.” \nوَاِذَا رَاَيْتَ الَّذِيْنَ يَخُوْضُوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا فَاَعْرِضْ عَنْهُمْ حَتّٰى يَخُوْضُوْا فِىْ حَدِيْثٍ غَيْرِهٖ ؕ وَاِمَّا يُنْسِيَنَّكَ الشَّيْطٰنُ فَلَا تَقْعُدْ بَعْدَ الذِّكْرٰى مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(68)\nWA EZAA RA-AYTA LAZEENA YAKHOOZOONA FEE AAYAATENAA FAAA’REZ A’NHUM HATTAA YAKHOOZOOA FEE HADEESIN GHAYREH WA AMMAA YUNSEENNAKA SHAYTAANO FALAA TAQU’UD BA’DA ZIKRAA LAAHA QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nWhen thou seest men engaged in vain discourse about Our signs, turn away from them unless they turn to a different theme. If Satan ever makes thee forget, then after recollection, sit not thou in the company of those who do wrong. \nوَمَا عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَ مِنْ حِسَابِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ وَّلٰكِنْ ذِكْرٰى لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(69)\nWA MAA A’LAL LAZEENA YATTAQOON MIN HESAABEHEM MIN SHAY-IN LAAKIL ZEKRAA LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\nOn their account no responsibility falls on the righteous, but (their duty) is to remind them, that they may (learn to) fear Allah. \nوَذَرِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ لَعِبًا وَّلَهْوًا وَّغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا وَ ذَكِّرْ بِهٖۤ اَنْ تُبْسَلَ نَفْسٌ ۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْۖ لَيْسَ لَهَا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلِىٌّ وَّلَا شَفِيْعٌ ۚ وَاِنْ تَعْدِلْ كُلَّ عَدْلٍ لَّا يُؤْخَذْ مِنْهَا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اُبْسِلُوْا بِمَا كَسَبُوْا ۚ لَهُمْ شَرَابٌ مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍ وَّعَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(70)\nWAZARE LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA DEENAHUM LAE’EBAN WWALAHWAN WWAGHARRATHUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA WA ZAKKER BEHI AN TUBSALA NAFSUN BEMAA KASABAT LAYSA LAHAA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WALIYYUN WA LAA SHAFEEA’UN WA TAA’DEL KULLA ZAWAY LAA YUKHAZ MINHAA OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA AUBSELOOA BEMAA KASABOO LAHUM SHARAABUN MIN HAMEEMIN WWAA’AZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM BEMAA KAANOO YAKFOROON.\nLeave alone those who take their religion to be mere play and amusement, and are deceived by the life of this world. But proclaim (to them) this (truth): that every soul delivers itself to ruin by its own acts: it will find for itself no protector or intercessor except Allah: if it offered every ransom, (or reparation), none will be accepted: such is (the end of) those who deliver themselves to ruin by their own acts: they will have for drink (only) boiling water, and for punishment, one most grievous: for they persisted in rejecting Allah. \nقُلْ اَنَدْعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُنَا وَلَا يَضُرُّنَا وَنُرَدُّ عَلٰٓى اَعْقَابِنَا بَعْدَ اِذْ هَدٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ كَالَّذِى اسْتَهْوَتْهُ الشَّيٰطِيْنُ فِى الْاَرْضِ حَيْرَانَ لَهٗۤ اَصْحٰبٌ يَّدْعُوْنَهٗۤ اِلَى الْهُدَى ائْتِنَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّ هُدَى اللّٰهِ هُوَ الْهُدٰىؕ وَاُمِرْنَا لِنُسْلِمَ لِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(71)\nQUL AANADU’OOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UNAA WA LAA YAZURRUNAA WANURADDU A’LAA AAA’QAABENAA BA’DA IZ HADAANAA LAAHO KA-LAZIS ASTAHWATHU SHAYAATEENO FIL ARZE HAYRAANA LAHU AASHAABUN YYADU’OONAH ELAL AL-HUDAA E-ATENAA QUL INNAL HODAL LAAHE HOWA HODAA WA WAAMERNAA LENUSLEMA LE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSay: “Shall we indeed call on others besides Allah, things that can do us neither good nor harm, and turn on our heels after receiving guidance from Allah? - like one whom the evil ones have made into a fool, wandering bewildered through the earth, his friends calling, come to us', (vainly) guiding him to the path.” Say: “Allah's guidance is the (only) guidance, and we have been directed to submit ourselves to the Lord of the worlds;- \nوَاَنْ اَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اتَّقُوْهُ ؕ وَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(72)\nWA AAQEEMOOA SALAATA WA ATTAQOOHU WA HOWA LAZEE ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\n“To establish regular prayers and to fear Allah: for it is to Him that we shall be gathered together.” \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّؕ وَيَوْمَ يَقُوْلُ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُؕ قَوْلُهُ الْحَقُّ ؕ وَلَهُ الْمُلْكُ يَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ ؕ عٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ وَ الشَّهَادَةِ ؕ وَهُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(73)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ WA YAWMA YAQOOLO KUN FAYAKOONU QAWLUHU HAQQO LAHUL A’LAYNAA YAWMA YUNFAKHO FIL SOORE A’ALEMUL GHAYBE WA ASH-SHAHAADATE WA HOWA HAKEEM KHABEER.\nIt is He who created the heavens and the earth in true (proportions): the day He saith, “Be,” behold! it is. His word is the truth. His will be the dominion the day the trumpet will be blown. He knoweth the unseen as well as that which is open. For He is the Wise, well acquainted (with all things). \nوَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ لِاَبِيْهِ اٰزَرَ اَتَتَّخِذُ اَصْنَامًا اٰلِهَةً  ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكَ وَقَوْمَكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(74)\nWA IZ QAALA AEBRAAHEEMU LEAABEEHE AAAZARA AATATTAKHEZU AASNAAMAN AALEHATAL INNEE AARAAKA WAQAWMAKA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\n Lo! Abraham said to his father Azar: “Takest thou idols for gods? For I see thee and thy people in manifest error.” \nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُرِىْۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ مَلَكُوْتَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلِيَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُوْقِنِيْنَ‏(75)\nWA KAZAALEKA NUREAA IBRAAHEEMA MALAKOOTA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA LEYAKOONA MENAL AL-MOOQENEENA.\nSo also did We show Abraham the power and the laws of the heavens and the earth, that he might (with understanding) have certitude. \nفَلَمَّا جَنَّ عَلَيْهِ الَّيْلُ رَاٰ كَوْكَبًا ۚ قَالَ هٰذَا رَبِّىْ ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَلَ قَالَ لَاۤ اُحِبُّ الْاٰفِلِيْنَ‏(76)\nFALAMMAA JANNA A’LAYHE LAYL RAA KAWKABAN QAALA HAAZAA RABBEE FALAMMAA AAFALA QAALA LAA AUHEBBU AL-AAAFELEENA.\nWhen the night covered him over, He saw a star: He said: “This is my Lord.” But when it set, He said: “I love not those that set.” \nفَلَمَّا رَاَالْقَمَرَ بَازِغًا قَالَ هٰذَا رَبِّىْ ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَلَ قَالَ لَئِنْ لَّمْ يَهْدِنِىْ رَبِّىْ لَاَ كُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الضَّآ لِّيْنَ‏(77)\nFALAMMAA RAAALQAMARA BAAZEGHAN QAALA HAAZAA RABBEE FALAMMAA AAFALA QAALA LAIL LAM YAHDENEAA RABBEE LAA KOONANNA MENAL QAWMIL LAMENAZ ZAAAL-LEEN.\nWhen he saw the moon rising in splendour, he said: “This is my Lord.” But when the moon set, He said: “unless my Lord guide me, I shall surely be among those who go astray.” \nفَلَمَّا رَاٰ الشَّمْسَ بَازِغَةً قَالَ هٰذَا رَبِّىْ هٰذَاۤ اَكْبَرُۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَلَتْ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(78)\nFALAMMAA RAA SHAMSA BAAZEGHATAN QAALA HAAZAA RABBEE HAAZAA AKBARO FALAMMAA AAFALAT QAALA LE-QAWMEHI INNEE BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUSHREKOONA.\nWhen he saw the sun rising in splendour, he said: “This is my Lord; this is the greatest (of all).” But when the sun set, he said: “O my people! I am indeed free from your (guilt) of giving partners to Allah. \nاِنِّىْ وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِىَ لِلَّذِىْ فَطَرَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ حَنِيْفًا وَّمَاۤ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَۚ‏(79)\nINNEE WAJJAHTU WAJHEAAA LIL-LAZEE FATARA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA HANEEFAA WA MAA ANAA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\n“For me, I have set my face, firmly and truly, towards Him Who created the heavens and the earth, and never shall I give partners to Allah.” \nوَحَآجَّهٗ قَوْمُهٗ ؕ قَالَ اَتُحَآجُّٓونِّىْ فِى اللّٰهِ وَقَدْ هَدٰٮنِؕ وَلَاۤ اَخَافُ مَا تُشْرِكُوْنَ بِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ رَبِّىْ شَيْئًا ؕ وَسِعَ رَبِّىْ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًاؕ اَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(80)\nWAHAAJJAH QAWMOHU QAALA AATUHAAJJOOONNEAA FIL LAAHE WA QAD HADAANE WA LAA AKHAAFO MAA TUSHREKOONA BEHI ILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL RABBEE SHAY-ANW WASEA’ RABBEE KULLA SHAY-IN E’ELMAN AFALAA TATAZAKKAROONA.\nHis people disputed with him. He said: “(Come) ye to dispute with me, about Allah, when He (Himself) hath guided me? I fear not (the beings) ye associate with Allah: Unless my Lord willeth, (nothing can happen). My Lord comprehendeth in His knowledge all things. Will ye not (yourselves) be admonished? \nوَكَيْفَ اَخَافُ مَاۤ اَشْرَكْتُمْ وَلَا تَخَافُوْنَ اَنَّكُمْ اَشْرَكْتُمْ بِاللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهٖ عَلَيْكُمْ سُلْطٰنًا ؕ فَاَىُّ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ اَحَقُّ بِالْاَمْنِۚ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَۘ‏(81)\nWA KAYFA AKHAAFO MAA AASHRAKTUM WA LAA TAKHAAFOONA ANNAKUM AASHRAKTUM BIL-LAAHE MAA LAM YUNAZZEL BEHI A’LAYKUM SULTAANAN FAAAAAU AL-FAREEQAYNE AHAQQO BIL-AAMNE IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\n“How should I fear (the beings) ye associate with Allah, when ye fear not to give partners to Allah without any warrant having been given to you? Which of (us) two parties hath more right to security? (tell me) if ye know. \nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَمْ يَلْبِسُوْۤا اِيْمَانَهُمْ بِظُلْمٍ اُولٰۤئِكَ لَهُمُ الْاَمْنُ وَهُمْ مُّهْتَدُوْنَ‏(82)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA LAM YALBESOOA AEEMAANAHUM BEZULMIN AOOLAAEKA LAHOMUL AL-AAMNU WA HUM HUM MOHTADOON.\n“It is those who believe and confuse not their beliefs with wrong - that are (truly) in security, for they are on (right) guidance.” \nوَتِلْكَ حُجَّتُنَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖؕ نَرْفَعُ دَرَجٰتٍ مَّنْ نَّشَآءُ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(83)\nWA TILKAL HUJJATUNAA AAATAYNAAHAA IBRAAHEEMA A’LAA QAWMEH NARFAU’U DARAJAATIN MAN NNASHAAU INNAL RABBAKA HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nThat was the reasoning about Us, which We gave to Abraham (to use) against his people: We raise whom We will, degree after degree: for thy Lord is full of wisdom and knowledge. \nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَؕ كُلًّا هَدَيْنَا ۚ وَنُوْحًا هَدَيْنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَمِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهٖ دَاوٗدَ وَسُلَيْمٰنَ وَاَيُّوْبَ وَيُوْسُفَ وَمُوْسٰى وَ هٰرُوْنَؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُحْسِنِيْنَۙ‏(84)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WAYAA’QOOBA KULLAN HADAYNAA WA ARSALNAA HADAYNAA MIN QABLO WA MIN ZURREETEH DAAWOODA WA SOLAYMAANA WAAYYOOBA WAYOOSUFA WA MOOSAA WA HAAROONA WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MOHSENEEN.\nWe gave him Isaac and Jacob: all (three) guided: and before him, We guided Noah, and among his progeny, David, Solomon, Job, Joseph, Moses, and Aaron: thus do We reward those who do good: \nوَزَكَرِيَّا وَيَحْيٰى وَعِيْسٰى وَاِلْيَاسَؕ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَۙ‏(85)\nWAZAKAREEA WAYAHYAA WA E’ESAA WAALYAASA KULLUL MENAL SAALEHEEN.\nAnd Zakariya and John, and Jesus and Elias: all in the ranks of the righteous: \nوَاِسْمٰعِيْلَ وَالْيَسَعَ وَيُوْنُسَ وَلُوْطًا ؕ وَكُلًّا فَضَّلْنَا عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(86)\nWA ISMAA-E’ELA WAL YASAA’A WAYOONUSA WA LOOTAN WAKULLAN FAZZALNAA A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd Isma'il and Elisha, and Jonas, and Lot: and to all We gave favour above the nations: \nوَمِنْ اٰبَآئِهِمْ وَذُرِّيّٰتِهِمْ وَاِخْوَانِهِمْۚ وَاجْتَبَيْنٰهُمْ وَهَدَيْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(87)\nWA MIN AAABAAEHEM WAZURREETEHEM WAAKHWAANEHEM WAAJTABAYNAAHUM WAHADAYNAAHUM ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\n(To them) and to their fathers, and progeny and brethren: We chose them, and we guided them to a straight way. \nذٰ لِكَ هُدَى اللّٰهِ يَهْدِىْ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖؕ وَلَوْ اَشْرَكُوْا لَحَبِطَ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(88)\nZAA LEKA HODAL LAAHE YAHDEE BEHI MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’EBAADEH WA LAW ASHRAKOO LAHABETA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThis is the guidance of Allah: He giveth that guidance to whom He pleaseth, of His worshippers. If they were to join other gods with Him, all that they did would be vain for them. \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ ؕ فَاِنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِهَا هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ فَقَدْ وَكَّلْنَا بِهَا قَوْمًا لَّيْسُوْا بِهَا بِكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(89)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA WAL HUKMA WA NOBUWWATA FA-IN YAKFUR BEHAA HAAOOLAAA-E FAQAD WAKKALNAA BEHAA QAWMAN LLAYSOOA BEHAA BE-KAAFEREEN.\nThese were the men to whom We gave the Book, and authority, and prophethood: if these (their descendants) reject them, Behold! We shall entrust their charge to a new people who reject them not. \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ هَدَى اللّٰهُ فَبِهُدٰٮهُمُ اقْتَدِهْ ؕ قُلْ لَّاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا ؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٰى لِلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(90)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LAZEENA LAAHO FABEHUDAAHUMU AQTADEH QUL LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE AJRAN IN HOWA ILLAA ZEKRAA LIL-A’AALAMEENA.\nThose were the (prophets) who received Allah's guidance: Copy the guidance they received; Say: “No reward for this do I ask of you: This is no less than a message for the nations.” \nوَمَا قَدَرُوا اللّٰهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهٖۤ اِذْ قَالُوْا مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى بَشَرٍ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ ؕ قُلْ مَنْ اَنْزَلَ الْكِتٰبَ الَّذِىْ جَآءَ بِهٖ مُوْسٰى نُوْرًا وَّ هُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ تَجْعَلُوْنَهٗ قَرَاطِيْسَ تُبْدُوْنَهَا وَتُخْفُوْنَ كَثِيْرًا ۚ وَعُلِّمْتُمْ مَّا لَمْ تَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنْتُمْ وَلَاۤ اٰبَآؤُكُمْؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُۙ ثُمَّ ذَرْهُمْ فِىْ خَوْضِهِمْ يَلْعَبُوْنَ‏(91)\nWA MAA QADAROOA LAAHA HAQQA QADREH IZ QAALOO MAA ANZALAL LAAHO A’LAA BASHARIN MIN SHAY-IN QUL MAN ANZALAL KETAABA LAZEE JAAA-A BEHI MOOSAA NOORAN WA HODAM LIN-NAASE TAJA’ALOONAH QARAATEESA TUBDOONAHAA WA TUKHFOONA KASEERAA WAU’ULLEMTUM MAA LAM TA’LAMOO ANTUM WA LAA AAABAAUKUM QOLIL LAAHO SUMMA ZARHUM FEE KHAWZEHEM YALA’ABOONA.\nNo just estimate of Allah do they make when they say: “Nothing doth Allah send down to man (by way of revelation)” Say: “Who then sent down the Book which Moses brought? a light and guidance to man: But ye make it into (separate) sheets for show, while ye conceal much (of its contents): therein were ye taught that which ye knew not- neither ye nor your fathers.” Say: “Allah (sent it down)”: Then leave them to plunge in vain discourse and trifling. \nوَهٰذَا كِتٰبٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ مُبٰرَكٌ مُّصَدِّقُ الَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَلِتُنْذِرَ اُمَّ الْقُرٰى وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ وَهُمْ عَلٰى صَلَاتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُوْنَ‏(92)\nWA KETAABUM ANZALNAAHO MUBAARAKUN MMUSADDEQU LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WA LETUNZERA AUMMA KORAA WA MAN HAWLAHAA WAL LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE YOAMENOONA BEHI WA HUM A’LAA SALAATEHIM YUHAAFEZOONA.\nAnd this is a Book which We have sent down, bringing blessings, and confirming (the revelations) which came before it: that thou mayest warn the mother of cities and all around her. Those who believe in the Hereafter believe in this (Book), and they are constant in guarding their prayers. \nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ قَالَ اُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ وَلَمْ يُوْحَ اِلَيْهِ شَىْءٌ وَّمَنْ قَالَ سَاُنْزِلُ مِثْلَ مَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُؕ وَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ فِىْ غَمَرٰتِ الْمَوْتِ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ بَاسِطُوْۤا اَيْدِيْهِمْۚ اَخْرِجُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمُؕ اَلْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ عَذَابَ الْهُوْنِ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ غَيْرَ الْحَقِّ وَكُنْتُمْ عَنْ اٰيٰتِهٖ تَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW QAALA OOHEYA ELAYYA WA LAM YOOHA ELAYHE SHAY-UN WWAMAN QAALA SAANZELU MISLA MAA ANZALAL LAAH WA LAW TARAAA EZIM ZAALEMOON FEE GHAMARAATE MAWT WAL MALAAA-EKATO BAASETOOA AYDEEHIM AKHREJOO AANFUSAKUMU AL-YAWMA TUJZAWNA A’ZAABAL HOONE BEMAA KUNTUM TAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE GHAYRA HAQQE WA KUNTUM A’N AAYAATEHI TASTAKBEROONA.\nWho can be more wicked than one who inventeth a lie against Allah, or saith, “I have received inspiration,” when he hath received none, or (again) who saith, “I can reveal the like of what Allah hath revealed”? If thou couldst but see how the wicked (do fare) in the flood of confusion at death! - the angels stretch forth their hands, (saying),”Yield up your souls: this day shall ye receive your reward, a penalty of shame, for that ye used to tell lies against Allah, and scornfully to reject of His signs!” \nوَلَقَدْ جِئْتُمُوْنَا فُرَادٰى كَمَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّتَرَكْتُمْ مَّا خَوَّلْنٰكُمْ وَرَآءَ ظُهُوْرِكُمْۚ وَمَا نَرٰى مَعَكُمْ شُفَعَآءَكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ اَنَّهُمْ فِيْكُمْ شُرَكٰٓؤُا ؕ لَقَدْ تَّقَطَّعَ بَيْنَكُمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْكُمْ مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَزْعُمُوْنَ‏(94)\nWA LAQAD JETUMOONAA FURAADAA KAMAA KHALAQNAAKUM AWWALA MARRAH WWATARAKTUM MAA KHAWLNAAKUM WARAAA-A ZUHOOREKUM WA MAA NARAA MA-A’KUM SHUFAA’AAAKUMU LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM ANNAHUM FEEKUM SHURAKAAAUA LAQAD TTAQATTAA’A BAYNAKUM WA ZALLA A’NKUM MAA KUNTUM TAZ-O’MOON.\n“And behold! ye come to us bare and alone as We created you for the first time: ye have left behind you all (the favours) which We bestowed on you: We see not with you your intercessors whom ye thought to be partners in your affairs: so now all relations between you have been cut off, and your (pet) fancies have left you in the lurch!” \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ فَالِقُ الْحَبِّ وَالنَّوٰىؕ يُخْرِجُ الْحَىَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَمُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتِ مِنَ الْحَىِّ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ فَاَنّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(95)\nINNAL LAAHA FAALEQU AL-HABBE WAALNNAWAA KHAB-A HAYYA MENAL MAYYETE WA WAMUKHREJU MAYYETE WA MENAL HAYYE ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO FA-ANNAA TUFAKOONA.\n It is Allah Who causeth the seed-grain and the date-stone to split and sprout. He causeth the living to issue from the dead, and He is the one to cause the dead to issue from the living. That is Allah: then how are ye deluded away from the truth? \nفَالِقُ الْاِصْبَاحِۚ وَ جَعَلَ الَّيْلَ سَكَنًا وَّالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ حُسْبَانًا ؕ ذٰلِكَ تَقْدِيْرُ الْعَزِيْزِ الْعَلِيْمِ‏(96)\nFAALEQU AL-AESBAAHE WA JA-A’LA LAYLA SAKANAN WWAALSSHAMSA WAL QAMARA HUSBAANAN ZAALEKA TAQDEERUL A’ZEEZIL AL-A’ALEEME.\nHe it is that cleaveth the day-break (from the dark): He makes the night for rest and tranquillity, and the sun and moon for the reckoning (of time): Such is the judgment and ordering of (Him), the Exalted in Power, the Omniscient. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ النُّجُوْمَ لِتَهْتَدُوْا بِهَا فِىْ ظُلُمٰتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِؕ قَدْ فَصَّلْنَا الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(97)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL AN-NUJOOMA LE-NASAARAA BEHAA FEE ZOLOMAATIL BARRE WAL BAHRE QAD FASSALNAA AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nIt is He Who maketh the stars (as beacons) for you, that ye may guide yourselves, with their help, through the dark spaces of land and sea: We detail Our signs for people who know. \nوَ هُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ فَمُسْتَقَرٌّ وَّمُسْتَوْدَعٌ ؕ قَدْ فَصَّلْنَا الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّفْقَهُوْنَ‏(98)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AN-SHA-A MIN NAFSIN WWAAHEDATIN FA MUSTAQARRUNW WWAMUSTAWDAA’UN QAD FASSALNAA AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YYAFQAHOONA.\nIt is He Who hath produced you from a single person: here is a place of sojourn and a place of departure: We detail Our signs for people who understand. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً ۚ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖ نَبَاتَ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ فَاَخْرَجْنَا مِنْهُ خَضِرًا نُّخْرِجُ مِنْهُ حَبًّا مُّتَرَاكِبًا ۚ وَمِنَ النَّخْلِ مِنْ طَلْعِهَا قِنْوَانٌ دَانِيَةٌ وَّجَنّٰتٍ مِّنْ اَعْنَابٍ وَّالزَّيْتُوْنَ وَالرُّمَّانَ مُشْتَبِهًا وَّغَيْرَ مُتَشَابِهٍ ؕ اُنْظُرُوْۤا اِلٰى ثَمَرِهٖۤ اِذَاۤ اَثْمَرَ وَيَنْعِهٖ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكُمْ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(99)\nWA HOWA LAZEE ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA AKH-RAJNAA BEHI NABAATA KULLE SHAY-IN FA AKH-RAJNAA MINHO KHAZERAN NNUKHREJU MINHO HABBANW MMUTARAAKEBAN WA MENAN AN-NAKHLE MIN TALE’EHAA QENWAANUN DAANEETUN WA MIN AAA’NAABIN WWAALZZAYTOONA WAALRRUMMAANA MUSHTABEHAN WWAGHAYRA MUTASHAABEHIN AUNZUROOA ELAA SAMAREHI EZAA AASMARA WAYANE’EH INNAL FEE ZAA ZAALEKUM LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nIt is He Who sendeth down rain from the skies: with it We produce vegetation of all kinds: from some We produce green (crops), out of which We produce grain, heaped up (at harvest); out of the date-palm and its sheaths (or spathes) (come) clusters of dates hanging low and near: and (then there are) gardens of grapes, and olives, and pomegranates, each similar (in kind) yet different (in variety): when they begin to bear fruit, feast your eyes with the fruit and the ripeness thereof. Behold! in these things there are signs for people who believe. \nوَجَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ الْجِنَّ وَخَلَقَهُمْ وَخَرَقُوْا لَهٗ بَنِيْنَ وَبَنٰتٍۢ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(100)\nWA JA-A’LOO LILLAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A AL-JENNA WA KHALAQAHUM WAKHARAQOOA LAHU BANEENA WABANAATIN BEGHAYRIL E’ELMIN WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nYet they make the Jinns equals with Allah, though Allah did create the Jinns; and they falsely, having no knowledge, attribute to Him sons and daughters. Praise and glory be to Him! (for He is) above what they attribute to Him! \nبَدِيْعُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ اَنّٰى يَكُوْنُ لَهٗ وَلَدٌ وَّلَمْ تَكُنْ لَّهٗ صَاحِبَةٌ ؕ وَخَلَقَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ ۚ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(101)\nBADEE-U’S SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ ANNAA LAHUL LAHU WALADUN LAM TAKUN LAHU SAAHEBATUN WA KHALAQAL KULLA SHAY-IN WA HOWA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nTo Him is due the primal origin of the heavens and the earth: How can He have a son when He hath no consort? He created all things, and He hath full knowledge of all things. \nذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ فَاعْبُدُوْهُۚ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّكِيْلٌ‏(102)\nZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN FAAA’BUDOOHU WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAKEELUN.\nThat is Allah, your Lord! there is no god but He, the Creator of all things: then worship ye Him: and He hath power to dispose of all affairs. \nلَا تُدْرِكُهُ الْاَبْصَارُ وَهُوَ يُدْرِكُ الْاَبْصَارَۚ وَهُوَ اللَّطِيْفُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(103)\nLAA TUDREKUHU IZ ZAAGHATIL WA HOWA YUDREKU AL-AABSAARA WA HOWA LATEEFUL KHABEER.\nNo vision can grasp Him, but His grasp is over all vision: He is above all comprehension, yet is acquainted with all things. \nقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بَصَآئِرُ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْۚ فَمَنْ اَبْصَرَ فَلِنَفْسِهٖ ۚ وَمَنْ عَمِىَ فَعَلَيْهَا ؕ وَمَاۤ اَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ بِحَفِيْظٍ‏(104)\nQAD JAAA-AKUM BASAAERU MIN RABBEKUM FAMAN AABSARA FALENAFSEH WA MAN A’AMEAAA FA A’LAYHAA WA MAA ANAA A’LAYKUM BEHAFEEZIN.\n“Now have come to you, from your Lord, proofs (to open your eyes): if any will see, it will be for (the good of) his own soul; if any will be blind, it will be to his own (harm): I am not (here) to watch over your doings.” \nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ وَلِيَقُوْلُوْا دَرَسْتَ وَلِنُبَيِّنَهٗ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(105)\nWA KAZAALEKA NUSARREFU AAYAATE WALEEQOOLOOA DARASTA WALENUBAYNAH LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nThus do we explain the signs by various (symbols): that they may say, “Thou hast taught (us) diligently,” and that We may make the matter clear to those who know. \nاِتَّبِعْ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ وَاَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(106)\nAETTABEA’ MAA OOHEYA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA WAAA’REZ A’NIL MUSHREKEEN.\nFollow what thou art taught by inspiration from thy Lord: there is no god but He: and turn aside from those who join gods with Allah. \nوَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَاۤ اَشْرَكُوْا ؕ وَمَا جَعَلْنٰكَ عَلَيْهِمْ حَفِيْظًا ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِوَكِيْلٍ‏(107)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA ASHRAKOO WA MAA JAA’ALNAAKA A’LAYHIM HAFEEZAN WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEWAKEELIN.\nIf it had been Allah's plan, they would not have taken false gods: but We made thee not one to watch over their doings, nor art thou set over them to dispose of their affairs. \nوَلَا تَسُبُّوا الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ فَيَسُبُّوا اللّٰهَ عَدْوًاۢ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ زَيَّنَّا لِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ عَمَلَهُمْ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ مَّرْجِعُهُمْ فَيُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(108)\nWA LAA TASUBBOOA LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE FAYASUBBOOA LAAHA A’ADWAN BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN KAZAALEKA ZAYYANNAA LEKULLIM UMMATIN A’AMALAHUM SUMMA ELAA RABBEHIM MMARJEU’UHUM FAYUNABBEUHUM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nRevile not ye those whom they call upon besides Allah, lest they out of spite revile Allah in their ignorance. Thus have We made alluring to each people its own doings. In the end will they return to their Lord, and We shall then tell them the truth of all that they did. \nوَاَقْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ لَئِنْ جَآءَتْهُمْ اٰيَةٌ لَّيُؤْمِنُنَّ بِهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا الْاٰيٰتُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَمَا يُشْعِرُكُمْۙ اَنَّهَاۤ اِذَا جَآءَتْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(109)\nWAAQSAMOOA BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AAYMAANEHEM LAIL JAAA-AHUM TAA-TEENAA LLAYUMENUNNA BEHAA QUL INNAMAA AAYAATO I’NDAL LAAHE WA MAA YUSHE’ERUKUM AANNAHAA EZAA JAAA-AT LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThey swear their strongest oaths by Allah, that if a (special) sign came to them, by it they would believe. Say: “Certainly (all) signs are in the power of Allah: but what will make you (Muslims) realise that (even) if (special) signs came, they will not believe.”? \nوَنُقَلِّبُ اَفْئِدَتَهُمْ وَاَبْصَارَهُمْ كَمَا لَمْ يُؤْمِنُوْا بِهٖۤ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ وَّنَذَرُهُمْ فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(110)\nWANUQALLEBU AAFEDATAHUM WAABSAARAHUM KAMAA LAM YOAMENOO BEHI AWWALA MARRAH WWANAZARUHUM FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nWe (too) shall turn to (confusion) their hearts and their eyes, even as they refused to believe in this in the first instance: We shall leave them in their trespasses, to wander in distraction. \nوَلَوْ اَنَّنَا نَزَّلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ وَكَلَّمَهُمُ الْمَوْتٰى وَ حَشَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ قُبُلًا مَّا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ يَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(111)\nWA LAW AANNANAA NAZZALNAA ELAYHEMUS AL-MALAAAEKATA WAKALLAMAHUMU MAWTAA WA HASHARNAA A’LAYHIM KULLA SHAY-IN QUBULAN MAA KAANOO LE-YOAMENOO ILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL LAAHO LAAKINNAL AKSARAHUM YAJHALOONA.\nEven if We did send unto them angels, and the dead did speak unto them, and We gathered together all things before their very eyes, they are not the ones to believe, unless it is in Allah's plan. But most of them ignore (the truth). \nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِىٍّ عَدُوًّا شَيٰطِيْنَ الْاِنْسِ وَالْجِنِّ يُوْحِىْ بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضٍ زُخْرُفَ الْقَوْلِ غُرُوْرًا ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ مَا فَعَلُوْهُ فَذَرْهُمْ وَمَا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(112)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAA LEKULLIM NABEAAAIN A’DUWWAL SHAYTEENA AL-AENSE WA JINNE YOOHEAA KHALAA ELAA ELAA ZUKHRUFA AL-QAWLE GHOROORAA WA LAW SHAAA-AL RABBOKA MAA FAA’ALOOHU FAZARHUM WA MAA YAFTAROON.\nLikewise did We make for every Messenger an enemy, evil ones among men and jinns, inspiring each other with flowery discourses by way of deception. If thy Lord had so planned, they would not have done it: so leave them and their inventions alone. \nوَلِتَصْغٰٓى اِلَيْهِ اَفْئِدَةُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ وَلِيَرْضَوْهُ وَلِيَقْتَرِفُوْا مَا هُمْ مُّقْتَرِفُوْنَ‏(113)\nWALETASGHAAA ELAYHE AAFEDATU LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE WALEERZAWHU WALEEQTAREFOOA MAA HUM MMUQTAREFOONA.\nTo such (deceit) let the hearts of those incline, who have no faith in the hereafter: let them delight in it, and let them earn from it what they may. \nاَفَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَبْتَغِىْ حَكَمًا وَّهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْزَلَ اِلَيْكُمُ الْكِتٰبَ مُفَصَّلاً ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّهٗ مُنَزَّلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ بِالْحَقِّ فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِيْنَ‏(114)\nAAFAGHAYRA LAAHE AABTAGHEAA HAKAMAN WA LAZEE ANZALAL AELAYKUMU KETAABA MUFASSALAAN WAL LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YA’LAMOON ANNAHU MUNAZZALUN MIN RABBEKA BIL-HAQQE FALAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUMTAREEN.\nSay: “Shall I seek for judge other than Allah? - when He it is Who hath sent unto you the Book, explained in detail.” They know full well, to whom We have given the Book, that it hath been sent down from thy Lord in truth. Never be then of those who doubt. \nوَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ صِدْقًا وَّعَدْلاً  ؕ لَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمٰتِهٖ ۚ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(115)\nWATAMMAT KALEMATU RABBEKA SEDQAN WWAA’ADLAAN LAA MUBADDELA LEKALEMAATEH WA HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nThe word of thy Lord doth find its fulfilment in truth and in justice: None can change His words: for He is the one who heareth and knoweth all. \nوَاِنْ تُطِعْ اَكْثَرَ مَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ يُضِلُّوْكَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَاِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَخْرُصُوْنَ‏(116)\nWA TO-TE’ AKSARAN MAN FIL ARZE YUZELLOOKA A’N SABEELIL LAAH IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA HUM ILLAA YAKHRUSOONA.\nWert thou to follow the common run of those on earth, they will lead thee away from the way of Allah. They follow nothing but conjecture: they do nothing but lie. \nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ مَنْ يَّضِلُّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖۚ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(117)\nINNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO MAN YYAZELLU A’N SABEELEH WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BILMOHTADEEN.\nThy Lord knoweth best who strayeth from His way: He knoweth best who they are that receive His guidance. \nفَكُلُوْا مِمَّا ذُكِرَ اسْمُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ بِاٰيٰتِهٖ مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(118)\nFA-KOLOO MIMMAA ZUKERA RABBEKA LAAHE A’LAYHE IN KUNTUM BE-AAYAATEHI MUMENEENA.\nSo eat of (meats) on which Allah's name hath been pronounced, if ye have faith in His signs. \nوَمَا لَكُمْ اَلَّا تَاْكُلُوْا مِمَّا ذُكِرَ اسْمُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ وَقَدْ فَصَّلَ لَكُمْ مَّا حَرَّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ اِلَّا مَا اضْطُرِرْتُمْ اِلَيْهِؕ وَاِنَّ كَثِيْرًا لَّيُضِلُّوْنَ بِاَهْوَآئِهِمْ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُعْتَدِيْنَ‏(119)\nWA MAA LAKUM ALLAA TAAKULOOA MIMMAA ZUKERA RABBEKA LAAHE A’LAYHE WA QAD FASSALA LAKUM MAA HARRAMA A’LAYKUM ILLAA MAA AZTURERTUM AELAYHE WA INNA KASEERAA LLAYUZELLOONA BEAAHWAAEHEM BEGHAYRIL E’ELMIN INNAL RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BE-MO’TADEEN.\nWhy should ye not eat of (meats) on which Allah's name hath been pronounced, when He hath explained to you in detail what is forbidden to you - except under compulsion of necessity? But many do mislead (men) by their appetites unchecked by knowledge. Thy Lord knoweth best those who transgress. \nوَذَرُوْا ظَاهِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَبَاطِنَهٗؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ یَکْسِبُوْنَ الْاِثْمَ سَيُجْزَوْنَ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَقْتَرِفُوْنَ‏(120)\nWA ZAROO ZAAHERA AL-AESME WABAATENAH INNAL LAZEENA SEBOONA AL-AESMA SAYUJZAWNA BEMAA KAANOO YAQTAREFOONA.\nEschew all sin, open or secret: those who earn sin will get due recompense for their “earnings.” \nوَلَا تَاْكُلُوْا مِمَّا لَمْ يُذْكَرِ اسْمُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ وَاِنَّهٗ لَفِسْقٌ ؕ وَاِنَّ الشَّيٰطِيْنَ لَيُوْحُوْنَ اِلٰٓى اَوْلِيٰٓئِهِمْ لِيُجَادِلُوْكُمْ ۚ وَاِنْ اَطَعْتُمُوْهُمْ اِنَّكُمْ لَمُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(121)\nWA LAA TAAKULOOA MIMMAA LAM YUZKARE RABBEKA LAAHE A’LAYHE WA INNAHU LAFESQUN WA INNA SHAYAATEENA LAYOOHOONA ELAA AAWLEEEHEM LEEJAADELOOKUM WA AATAA’TUMOOHUM INNAKUM LAMUSHREKOONA.\nEat not of (meats) on which Allah's name hath not been pronounced: That would be impiety. But the evil ones ever inspire their friends to contend with you if ye were to obey them, ye would indeed be Pagans. \nاَوَمَنْ كَانَ مَيْتًا فَاَحْيَيْنٰهُ وَجَعَلْنَا لَهٗ نُوْرًا يَّمْشِىْ بِهٖ فِى النَّاسِ كَمَنْ مَّثَلُهٗ فِى الظُّلُمٰتِ لَيْسَ بِخَارِجٍ مِّنْهَا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(122)\nAAWAMAN KAANA MAYTAN FAAHYAYNAAHU WA JA-A’LNAA LAHU NOORAN YAMSHEE BEHI FIL NAASE KAMAM MMASALUH FIL ZOLOMAATE LAYSA BEKHAAREJIN MINHAA KAZAALEKA ZUYYENA LIL KAAFEREENA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nCan he who was dead, to whom We gave life, and a light whereby he can walk amongst men, be like him who is in the depths of darkness, from which he can never come out? Thus to those without faith their own deeds seem pleasing. \nوَكَذٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا فِىْ كُلِّ قَرْيَةٍ اَكٰبِرَ مُجْرِمِيْهَا لِيَمْكُرُوْا فِيْهَا ؕ وَمَا يَمْكُرُوْنَ اِلَّا بِاَنْفُسِهِمْ وَمَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(123)\nWA KAZAALEKA JA-A’LNAA FEE KULLE QARYATINW AAKAABERA MUJREMEEHAA LEEMKUROOA FEEHAA WA MAA YAMKOROON ILLAA BE-ANFOSEHIM WA MAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThus have We placed leaders in every town, its wicked men, to plot (and burrow) therein: but they only plot against their own souls, and they perceive it not. \nوَاِذَا جَآءَتْهُمْ اٰيَةٌ قَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ حَتّٰى نُؤْتٰى مِثْلَ مَاۤ اُوْتِىَ رُسُلُ اللّٰهِؔۘؕ اَللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ حَيْثُ يَجْعَلُ رِسٰلَتَهٗ ؕ سَيُصِيْبُ الَّذِيْنَ اَجْرَمُوْا صَغَارٌ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَعَذَابٌ شَدِيْدٌۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(124)\nWA EZAA JAAA-AHUM TAA-TEENAA QAALOO LAN NOAMENA HATTAA NUTAA MISLA MAA OOTEYA RUSULU AL-LAAHE ALLAAHO A-A’LAMO HAYSO YAJA’ALU RESAALATAH SAYUSEEBU LAZEENA AJRAMOO SAGHAARUN I’NDAL LAAHE WA A’ZAABUN SHADEEDUN BEMAA KAANOO YAMKOROON.\nWhen there comes to them a sign (from Allah), They say: “We shall not believe until we receive one (exactly) like those received by Allah's messengers.” Allah knoweth best where (and how) to carry out His mission. Soon will the wicked be overtaken by humiliation before Allah, and a severe punishment, for all their plots. \nفَمَنْ يُّرِدِ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّهْدِيَهٗ يَشْرَحْ صَدْرَهٗ لِلْاِسْلَامِۚ وَمَنْ يُّرِدْ اَنْ يُّضِلَّهٗ يَجْعَلْ صَدْرَهٗ ضَيِّقًا حَرَجًا كَاَنَّمَا يَصَّعَّدُ فِى السَّمَآءِؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَجْعَلُ اللّٰهُ الرِّجْسَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(125)\nFAMAN YYUREDE LAAHO AN YYAHDEEH YASHRAH SADRAH LIL-AESLAAME WA MAN YYURED AN YYUZELLAH YAJ-A’L SADRAH ZAYQAN HARAJAN KA-ANNAMAA YASSAAA’ADU FIL AS-SAMAAE KAZAALEKA YAJA’ALU LAAHO A’NKOMUR A’LAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThose whom Allah (in His plan) willeth to guide, He openeth their breast to Islam; those whom He willeth to leave straying, He maketh their breast close and constricted, as if they had to climb up to the skies: thus doth Allah (heap) the penalty on those who refuse to believe. \nوَهٰذَا صِرَاطُ رَبِّكَ مُسْتَقِيْمًا ؕ قَدْ فَصَّلْنَا الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(126)\nWA SERAATU RABBEKA MUSTAQEEMAN QAD FASSALNAA AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YYAZZAKKAROONA.\nThis is the way of thy Lord, leading straight: We have detailed the signs for those who receive admonition. \nلَهُمْ دَارُ السَّلٰمِ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ وَهُوَ وَلِيُّهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(127)\nLAHUM DAARU AS-SALAAME I’NDAL RABBEHIM WA HOWA WALEEHUM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\n For them will be a home of peace in the presence of their Lord: He will be their friend, because they practised (righteousness). \nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ۚ يٰمَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ قَدِ اسْتَكْثَرْتُمْ مِّنَ الْاِنْسِۚ وَقَالَ اَوْلِيٰٓئُهُمْ مِّنَ الْاِنْسِ رَبَّنَا اسْتَمْتَعَ بَعْضُنَا بِبَعْضٍ وَّبَلَغْنَاۤ اَجَلَنَا الَّذِىْۤ اَجَّلْتَ لَنَا ؕ قَالَ النَّارُ مَثْوٰٮكُمْ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(128)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A YAA JINNE QADE ASTAKSARTUM MENAL AL-AENSE WA QAALA AAWLEEUHUM MENAL AL-AENSE RABBANAA ASTAMTAA’A BAA’ZUNAA BE-BA’Z WWABALAGHNAA AAJALANAA LAZEE AAJJALTA LANAA QAALA TAMASSANAN MASWAAKUM KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ILLAA MAA SHAAA-ALLAAH INNAL RABBAKA HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nOne day will He gather them all together, (and say): “O ye assembly of Jinns! Much (toll) did ye take of men.” Their friends amongst men will say: “Our Lord! we made profit from each other: but (alas!) we reached our term - which thou didst appoint for us.” He will say: “The Fire be your dwelling-place: you will dwell therein for ever, except as Allah willeth.” for thy Lord is full of wisdom and knowledge. \nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُوَلِّىْ بَعْضَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بَعْضًاۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(129)\nWA KAZAALEKA NOOLLEAA YAWM ZAALEMEEN BA’ZAN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nThus do we make the wrong-doers turn to each other, because of what they earn. \nيٰمَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ اَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْكُمْ يَقُصُّوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِىْ وَيُنْذِرُوْنَكُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا ؕ قَالُوْا شَهِدْنَا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِنَا وَغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا وَشَهِدُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(130)\nYAA JINNE WAL INSE ALAM YAATEKUM RUSULUN MINKUM YAQUSSOONA A’LAYKUM AAAYAATEAA WAYUNZEROONAKUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA QAALOO SHAHIDNAA A’LAA AANFUSENAA WAGHARRATHUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA WASHAHEDOOA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM ANNAHUM KAANOO KAAFEREEN.\n“O ye assembly of Jinns and men! came there not unto you messengers from amongst you, setting forth unto you My signs, and warning you of the meeting of this Day of yours?” They will say: “We bear witness against ourselves.” It was the life of this world that deceived them. So against themselves will they bear witness that they rejected Faith. \nذٰ لِكَ اَنْ لَّمْ يَكُنْ رَّبُّكَ مُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰى بِظُلْمٍ وَّاَهْلُهَا غٰفِلُوْنَ‏(131)\nZAA LEKA AN LAM YAKUL RRABBUKA MOHLEKAL KORAA BEZULMIN WWAAHLUHAA GHAAFELOON.\n(The messengers were sent) thus, for thy Lord would not destroy for their wrong-doing men's habitations whilst their occupants were unwarned. \nوَلِكُلٍّ دَرَجٰتٌ مِّمَّا عَمِلُوْا ؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(132)\nWA DARAJAATUN MIMMAA A’MELOO WA MAA RABBOKA BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA YA’MALOON.\nTo all are degrees (or ranks) according to their deeds: for thy Lord is not unmindful of anything that they do. \nوَرَبُّكَ الْغَنِىُّ ذُو الرَّحْمَةِ ؕ اِنْ يَّشَاْ يُذْهِبْكُمْ وَيَسْتَخْلِفْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِكُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُ كَمَاۤ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنْ ذُرِّيَّةِ قَوْمٍ اٰخَرِيْنَ ؕ‏(133)\nWA RABBOKA AL-GHANEAAAU ZUL AR-RAHMATE IN YYASHAA YUZHEBKUM WAYASTAKHLEF MIN BAA’DEKUM MAA YASHAAA KAMAA AN-SHA-A MIN ZURREETE QAWMIN AAKHEREEN.\nThy Lord is self-sufficient, full of Mercy: if it were His will, He could destroy you, and in your place appoint whom He will as your successors, even as He raised you up from the posterity of other people. \nاِنَّ مَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لَاٰتٍ ۙوَّمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(134)\nINNAL MAA TOO-A’DOON LAATIN WA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nAll that hath been promised unto you will come to pass: nor can ye frustrate it (in the least bit). \nقُلْ يٰقَوْمِ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْ اِنِّىْ عَامِلٌۚ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ مَنْ تَكُوْنُ لَهٗ عَاقِبَةُ الدَّارِؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(135)\nQUL LE-QAWMEHI AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNEE A’AAMELUN FA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON MAN TAKOONO LAHU A’AQEBATUL DAAR INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ ZAALEMOON.\nSay: “O my people! Do whatever ye can: I will do (my part): soon will ye know who it is whose end will be (best) in the Hereafter: certain it is that the wrong-doers will not prosper.” \nوَجَعَلُوْا لِلّٰهِ مِمَّا ذَرَاَ مِنَ الْحَرْثِ وَالْاَنْعَامِ نَصِيْبًا فَقَالُوْا هٰذَا لِلّٰهِ بِزَعْمِهِمْ وَهٰذَا لِشُرَكَآئِنَا ۚ فَمَا كَانَ لِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ فَلَا يَصِلُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ لِلّٰهِ فَهُوَ يَصِلُ اِلٰى شُرَكَآئِهِمْ ؕ سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(136)\nWA JA-A’LOO LILLAAHE MIMMAA ZARAA MENAL AL-HARSE WAL AANA’AAME NASEEBAN FA-QAALOO HAAZAA LILLAAHE BEZAA’MEHEM WA LESHURAKAAENAA FAMAA KAANA LE-SHORAKAAA-EHIM FALAA YASELU ELAL LAAHE WA MAA KAANA LILLAAHE FAHOWA YASELU ELAA SHORAKAAA-EHIM SAAA-A MAA YAHKUMOONA.\nOut of what Allah hath produced in abundance in tilth and in cattle, they assigned Him a share: they say, according to their fancies: “This is for Allah, and this” - for our “partners”! but the share of their” partners “reacheth not Allah, whilst the share of Allah reacheth their “partners” ! evil (and unjust) is their assignment! \nوَكَذٰلِكَ زَيَّنَ لِكَثِيْرٍ مِّنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ قَتْلَ اَوْلَادِهِمْ شُرَكَآؤُهُمْ لِيُرْدُوْهُمْ وَلِيَلْبِسُوْا عَلَيْهِمْ دِيْنَهُمْ ۚ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا فَعَلُوْهُ ؕ فَذَرْهُمْ وَمَا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(137)\nWA KAZAALEKA ZAYNA LE-KASEERIM MENAL MUSHREKEEN QATLA AAWLAADEHEM SHURAKAAUHUM LEERDOOHUM WALEELBESOOA A’LAYHIM DEENAHUM WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA FAA’ALOOHU FAZARHUM WA MAA YAFTAROON.\nEven so, in the eyes of most of the pagans, their “partners” made alluring the slaughter of their children, in order to lead them to their own destruction, and cause confusion in their religion. If Allah had willed, they would not have done so: But leave alone them and their inventions. \nوَقَالُوْا هٰذِهٖۤ اَنْعَامٌ وَّحَرْثٌ حِجْرٌ ۖ لَّا يَطْعَمُهَاۤ اِلَّا مَنْ نَّشَآءُ بِزَعْمِهِمْ وَاَنْعَامٌ حُرِّمَتْ ظُهُوْرُهَا وَاَنْعَامٌ لَّا يَذْكُرُوْنَ اسْمَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهَا افْتِرَآءً عَلَيْهِ ؕ سَيَجْزِيْهِمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(138)\nWA QAALOO HAAZEHI AANA’AAMUN WWAHARSUN HEJRUN LAA YATA’AMUHAA ILLAA MAN NNASHAAU BEZAA’MEHEM WAANA’AAMUN HURREMAT ZUHOORUHAA WAANA’AAMUN LAA YAZKUROONA KORISMA LAAHE A’LAYHAA AFTERAAAN A’LAYHE SAYAJZEEHEM BEMAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nAnd they say that such and such cattle and crops are taboo, and none should eat of them except those whom - so they say - We wish; further, there are cattle forbidden to yoke or burden, and cattle on which, (at slaughter), the name of Allah is not pronounced; - inventions against Allah's name: soon will He requite them for their inventions. \nوَقَالُوْا مَا فِىْ بُطُوْنِ هٰذِهِ الْاَنْعَامِ خَالِصَةٌ لِّذُكُوْرِنَا وَمُحَرَّمٌ عَلٰٓى اَزْوَاجِنَا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّكُنْ مَّيْتَةً فَهُمْ فِيْهِ شُرَكَآءُ ؕ سَيَجْزِيْهِمْ وَصْفَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ حَكِيْمٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(139)\nWA QAALOO MAA FEE BUTOONE HAAZEHE AL-AANA’AAME KHAALESATUN LLEZUKOORENAA WA MOHARRAMUM A’LAA AAZWAAJENAA WA YYAKUN MMAYTATAN FAHUM FEEHE SHURAKAAU SAYAJZEEHEM WASFAHUM INNAHU HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nThey say: “What is in the wombs of such and such cattle is specially reserved (for food) for our men, and forbidden to our women; but if it is still-born, then all have share therein. For their (false) attribution (of superstitions to Allah), He will soon punish them: for He is full of wisdom and knowledge. \nقَدْ خَسِرَ الَّذِيْنَ قَتَلُوْۤا اَوْلَادَهُمْ سَفَهًۢا بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ وَّحَرَّمُوْا مَا رَزَقَهُمُ اللّٰهُ افْتِرَآءً عَلَى اللّٰهِؕ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا وَمَا كَانُوْا مُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(140)\nQAD KHASERA LAZEENA QATALOOA AAWLAADAHUM SAFAHAN BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN WWAHARRAMOOA MAA RAZAQAHUMU LAAHO AFTERAAAN A’LAL LAAH QAD ZALLOOA WA MAA KAANOO MOHTADEEN.\nLost are those who slay their children, from folly, without knowledge, and forbid food which Allah hath provided for them, inventing (lies) against Allah. They have indeed gone astray and heeded no guidance. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَ جَنّٰتٍ مَّعْرُوْشٰتٍ وَّغَيْرَ مَعْرُوْشٰتٍ وَّالنَّخْلَ وَالزَّرْعَ مُخْتَلِفًا اُكُلُهٗ وَالزَّيْتُوْنَ وَالرُّمَّانَ مُتَشَابِهًا وَّغَيْرَ مُتَشَابِهٍ ؕ كُلُوْا مِنْ ثَمَرِهٖۤ اِذَاۤ اَثْمَرَ وَاٰتُوْا حَقَّهٗ يَوْمَ حَصَادِهٖ ۖ وَلَا تُسْرِفُوْا ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(141)\nWA HOWA LAZEE AANSHAA JANNAATIN MMAA’ROOSHAATIN WWAGHAYRA MAA’ROOSHAATIN WWAALNNAKHLA WAALZZARA’A MUKHTALEFAN AUKULUH WAALZZAYTOONA WAALRRUMMAANA MOTASHAA-BEHAA WWAGHAYRA MUTASHAABEHIN KOLOO MIN SAMAREHI EZAA AASMARA WAATOOA HAQQAHU YAWMA HASAADEH WA LAA TUSREFOOA INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL MUSREFEEN.\n It is He Who produceth gardens, with trellises and without, and dates, and tilth with produce of all kinds, and olives and pomegranates, similar (in kind) and different (in variety): eat of their fruit in their season, but render the dues that are proper on the day that the harvest is gathered. But waste not by excess: for Allah loveth not the wasters. \nوَ مِنَ الْاَنْعَامِ حَمُوْلَةً وَّفَرْشًا ؕ كُلُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ وَ لَا تَتَّبِعُوْا خُطُوٰتِ الشَّيْطٰنِ ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ ۙ‏(142)\nWA MENAL AL-AANA’AAME HAMOOLATAN WWAFARSHAN KOLOO MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO WA LAA TATTABE-O’O KHOTOWATIS SHAYTAANE INNAHU LAKUM A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nOf the cattle are some for burden and some for meat: eat what Allah hath provided for you, and follow not the footsteps of Satan: for he is to you and avowed enemy. \nثَمٰنِيَةَ اَزْوَاجٍ ۚ مِنَ الضَّاْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَمِنَ الْمَعْزِ اثْنَيْنِ ؕ قُلْ ءٰٓالذَّكَرَيْنِ حَرَّمَ اَمِ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ اَمَّا اشْتَمَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ اَرْحَامُ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ؕ نَبِّئُوْنِىْ بِعِلْمٍ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ ۙ‏(143)\nSAMAANEETA AZWAAJINW MENAL AZ-ZAANE NAYNE WA MENAN AL-MAA’ZE NAYNE QUL AAALZZAKARAYNE HARRAMA AMIL AL-AUNSAYAYNE AMMAA ASHTAMALAT A’LAYHE AARHAAMU AL-AUNSAYAYNE NABBEOONEAA BE-I’LMIN IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\n(Take) eight (head of cattle) in (four) pairs: of sheep a pair, and of goats a pair; say, hath He forbidden the two males, or the two females, or (the young) which the wombs of the two females enclose? Tell me with knowledge if ye are truthful: \nوَمِنَ الْاِبِلِ اثْنَيْنِ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ اثْنَيْنِ ؕ قُلْ ءٰٓالذَّكَرَيْنِ حَرَّمَ اَمِ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ اَمَّا اشْتَمَلَتْ عَلَيْهِ اَرْحَامُ الْاُنْثَيَيْنِ ؕ اَمْ كُنْتُمْ شُهَدَآءَ اِذْ وَصّٰٮكُمُ اللّٰهُ بِهٰذَا ۚ فَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا لِّيُضِلَّ النَّاسَ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمٍ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِى الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(144)\nWA MENAN AL-AEBELE NAYNE WA MENAN AL-BAQARE NAYNE QUL AAALZZAKARAYNE HARRAMA AMIL AL-AUNSAYAYNE AMMAA ASHTAMALAT A’LAYHE AARHAAMU AL-AUNSAYAYNE AM KUNTUM SHOHADAAA-A IZ WASSAAKUMU LAAHO BEHAAZAA FAMAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN LLEEZELLA NAASA BEGHAYRIL I’LMIN INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nOf camels a pair, and oxen a pair; say, hath He forbidden the two males, or the two females, or (the young) which the wombs of the two females enclose? - Were ye present when Allah ordered you such a thing? But who doth more wrong than one who invents a lie against Allah, to lead astray men without knowledge? For Allah guideth not people who do wrong. \nقُل لَّاۤ اَجِدُ فِىْ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ مُحَرَّمًا عَلٰى طَاعِمٍ يَّطْعَمُهٗۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ مَيْتَةً اَوْ دَمًا مَّسْفُوْحًا اَوْ لَحْمَ خِنْزِيْرٍ فَاِنَّهٗ رِجْسٌ اَوْ فِسْقًا اُهِلَّ لِغَيْرِ اللّٰهِ بِهٖۚ فَمَنِ اضْطُرَّ غَيْرَ بَاغٍ وَّلَا عَادٍ فَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(145)\nQUL LAA AAJEDU FEE MAA OOHEYA ELAYYA MUHARRAMAN A’LAA TAAE’EMIN YYATA’AMUH ILLAA AN YAKOONA MAYTATAN AW DAMAN MMASFOOHAN AW LAHMA KHENZEERIN FA-INNAHU REJSUN AW FESQAN OHILLA LE-GHAYRIL LAAHE BEHI FAMANE’ TURRA GHAYRA BAAGHINW WA LAA A’ADIN FA-INNAL RABBAKA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nSay: “I find not in the message received by me by inspiration any (meat) forbidden to be eaten by one who wishes to eat it, unless it be dead meat, or blood poured forth, or the flesh of swine, for it is an abomination - or, what is impious, (meat) on which a name has been invoked, other than Allah's”. But (even so), if a person is forced by necessity, without wilful disobedience, nor transgressing due limits, thy Lord is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَعَلَى الَّذِيْنَ هَادُوْا حَرَّمْنَا كُلَّ ذِىْ ظُفُرٍ ۚ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ وَالْغَنَمِ حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ شُحُوْمَهُمَاۤ اِلَّا مَا حَمَلَتْ ظُهُوْرُهُمَاۤ اَوِ الْحَوَايَاۤ اَوْ مَا اخْتَلَطَ بِعَظْمٍ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ جَزَيْنٰهُمْ بِبَغْيِهِمْ ۖ وَاِنَّا لَصٰدِقُوْنَ‏(146)\nWA LAZEENA HAADOO HARRAMNAA KULLA ZEE ZUFURIN WA MENAN AL-BAQARE WAL GHANAME HARRAMNAA A’LAYHIM SHUHOOMAHUMAA ILLAA MAA HAMALAT ZUHOORUHUMAA AWE’ AL-HAWAAYAA AW MAA AKHTALATA BEA’AZMIN ZAA LEKA JAZAYNAAHUM BEBAGHYEHEM WA INNAA LASAADEQOON.\nFor those who followed the Jewish Law, We forbade every (animal) with undivided hoof, and We forbade them that fat of the ox and the sheep, except what adheres to their backs or their entrails, or is mixed up with a bone: this in recompense for their wilful disobedience: for We are true (in Our ordinances). \nفَاِنْ كَذَّبُوْكَ فَقُلْ رَّبُّكُمْ ذُوْ رَحْمَةٍ وَّاسِعَةٍ ۚ وَلَا يُرَدُّ بَاْسُهٗ عَنِ الْقَوْمِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(147)\nFA-IN KAZZABOOKA FAQUL RRABBUKUM ZOO RAHMATIN WWAASEA’ATIN WA LAA YORADDO BAASUH A’NIL QAWMIL MUJREMEEN.\nIf they accuse thee of falsehood, say: “Your Lord is full of mercy all-embracing; but from people in guilt never will His wrath be turned back. \nسَيَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا لَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَاۤ اَشْرَكْنَا وَلَاۤ اٰبَآؤُنَا وَلَا حَرَّمْنَا مِنْ شَىْءٍ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ كَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ حَتّٰى ذَاقُوْا بَاْسَنَا ؕ قُلْ هَلْ عِنْدَكُمْ مِّنْ عِلْمٍ فَتُخْرِجُوْهُ لَنَا ؕ اِنْ تَتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَاِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا تَخْرُصُوْنَ‏(148)\nSA-YAQOOLO LAZEENA ASHRAKOO LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA AASHRAKNAA WA LAA AAABAAUNAA WA LAA HARRAMNAA MIN SHAY-IN KAZAALEKA KAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM HATTAA ZAAQOO BAASANAA QUL HAL E’ENDAKUM MIN I’LMIN FATUKHREJOOHU LANAA IN TATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA ANTUM ILLAA TAKHRUSOONA.\nThose who give partners (to Allah) will say: “If Allah had wished, we should not have given partners to Him nor would our fathers; nor should we have had any taboos.” So did their ancestors argue falsely, until they tasted of Our wrath. Say: “Have ye any (certain) knowledge? If so, produce it before us. Ye follow nothing but conjecture: ye do nothing but lie.” \nقُلْ فَلِلّٰهِ الْحُجَّةُ الْبَالِغَةُ ۚ فَلَوْ شَآءَ لَهَدٰٮكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(149)\nQUL FALILLAAHE AL-HUJJATU AL-BAALEGHATU FA LAW SHAAA-AL LAHADAAKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nSay: “With Allah is the argument that reaches home: if it had been His will, He could indeed have guided you all.” \nقُلْ هَلُمَّ شُهَدَآءَكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ يَشْهَدُوْنَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ حَرَّمَ هٰذَا ۚ فَاِنْ شَهِدُوْا فَلَا تَشْهَدْ مَعَهُمْ ۚ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ وَهُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(150)\nQUL HALUMMA SHUHADAAAKUMU LAZEENA YASHHADOONA ANNAL LAAHA HARRAMA HAAZAA FA-IN SHAHEDOOA FALAA TASHHAD MA-A’HUM WA LAA TATTABEA’ AAHWAAA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE WA HUM BE-RABBEHIM YAA’DELOONA.\nSay: “Bring forward your witnesses to prove that Allah did forbid so and so.” If they bring such witnesses, be not thou amongst them: Nor follow thou the vain desires of such as treat our signs as falsehoods, and such as believe not in the Hereafter: for they hold others as equal with their Guardian-Lord. \nقُلْ تَعَالَوْا اَتْلُ مَا حَرَّمَ رَبُّكُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ اَلَّا تُشْرِكُوْا بِهٖ شَيْئًا وَّبِالْوَالِدَيْنِ اِحْسَانًا ۚ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوْۤا اَوْلَادَكُمْ مِّنْ اِمْلَاقٍؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكُمْ وَاِيَّاهُمْ ۚ وَلَا تَقْرَبُوا الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ ۚ وَلَا تَقْتُلُوا النَّفْسَ الَّتِىْ حَرَّمَ اللّٰهُ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ وَصّٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(151)\nQUL TA-A’ALAW AATLU MAA HARRAMA RABBOKUM A’LAYKUM ALLAA TUSHREKOOA BEHI SHAY-ANW WWABEALWAALEDAYNE EHSAANANW WA LAA TAQTULOOA AWLAADAKUM MIN AEMLAAQIN NAHNO NARZUQUKUM WAAYYAAHUM WA LAA TAQRABOOA AL-FAWAAHESHA MAA ZAHARAL MINHAA WA MAA BATANA WA LAA TAQTULOOA AN-NAFSA LATEE HARRAMA LAAHO ILLAA BIL-HAQQE ZAA ZAALEKUM WASSAAKUM BEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\n Say: “Come, I will rehearse what Allah hath (really) prohibited you from”: Join not anything as equal with Him; be good to your parents; kill not your children on a plea of want;- We provide sustenance for you and for them;- come not nigh to shameful deeds. Whether open or secret; take not life, which Allah hath made sacred, except by way of justice and law: thus doth He command you, that ye may learn wisdom. \nوَلَا تَقْرَبُوْا مَالَ الْيَتِيْمِ اِلَّا بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ حَتّٰى يَبْلُغَ اَشُدَّهٗ ۚ وَاَوْفُوْا الْكَيْلَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ بِالْقِسْطِ ۚ لَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَا ۚ وَاِذَا قُلْتُمْ فَاعْدِلُوْا وَلَوْ كَانَ ذَا قُرْبٰى ۚ وَبِعَهْدِ اللّٰهِ اَوْفُوْا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ وَصّٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ ۙ‏(152)\nWA LAA TAQRABOOA MAALA AL-YATEEME ILLAA BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSANO HATTAA HATTAA ASHUDDAHU WA AWFOO AL-KAYLA WA MEEZAAN BIL QISTE LAA NUKALLEFU NAFSAN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA WA EZAA IZ QULTUM FAAA’DELOOA WA LAW KAANA ZAL QURBAA WABEA’AHDE LAAHE AAWFOOA ZAA ZAALEKUM WASSAAKUM BEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nAnd come not nigh to the orphan's property, except to improve it, until he attain the age of full strength; give measure and weight with (full) justice;- no burden do We place on any soul, but that which it can bear;- whenever ye speak, speak justly, even if a near relative is concerned; and fulfil the covenant of Allah: thus doth He command you, that ye may remember. \nوَاَنَّ هٰذَا صِرَاطِىْ مُسْتَقِيْمًا فَاتَّبِعُوْهُ ۚ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوْا السُّبُلَ فَتَفَرَّقَ بِكُمْ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ وَصّٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(153)\nWA ANNAL HAAZAA SERAATEAA MUSTAQEEMAN FAATTABEU’OOHU WA LAA TATTABE-O’O AS-SUBULA FA MAA BEKUM A’N SABEELEH ZAA ZAALEKUM WASSAAKUM BEHI LA-A’LLAKUM TATTAQOON.\nVerily, this is My way, leading straight: follow it: follow not (other) paths: they will scatter you about from His (great) path: thus doth He command you. that ye may be righteous. \nثُمَّ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ تَمَامًا عَلَى الَّذِىْۤ اَحْسَنَ وَتَفْصِيْلاً لِّكُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُدًى وَرَحْمَةً لَّعَلَّهُمْ بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّهِمْ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(154)\nSUMMA AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA TAMAAMAN A’LAL LAZEE AHSANAL WATAFSEELAAN LEKULLE SHAY-IN WWAHUDAN WA RAHMATAM LA-A’LLAHUM BELEQAAE RABBEHIM YOAMENOONA.\nMoreover, We gave Moses the Book, completing (Our favour) to those who would do right, and explaining all things in detail, and a guide and a mercy, that they might believe in the meeting with their Lord. \nوَهٰذَا كِتٰبٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ مُبٰرَكٌ فَاتَّبِعُوْهُ وَاتَّقُوْا لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَۙ‏(155)\nWA KETAABUM ANZALNAAHO MUBAARAKUN FAATTABEU’OOHU WAT TAQOO LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nAnd this is a Book which We have revealed as a blessing: so follow it and be righteous, that ye may receive mercy: \nاَنْ تَقُوْلُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ الْكِتٰبُ عَلٰى طَآئِفَتَيْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِنَا وَاِنْ كُنَّا عَنْ دِرَاسَتِهِمْ لَغٰفِلِيْنَۙ‏(156)\nAN TAQOOLOO INNAMAA UNZELA KETAABO A’LAA TAAEFATAYNE MIN LAA WA KUNNAA A’N DERAASATEHEM LAGHAAFELEENA.\nLest ye should say: “The Book was sent down to two Peoples before us, and for our part, we remained unacquainted with all that they learned by assiduous study:” \nاَوْ تَقُوْلُوْا لَوْ اَنَّاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْنَا الْكِتٰبُ لَكُنَّاۤ اَهْدٰى مِنْهُمْ ۚ فَقَدْ جَآءَكُمْ بَيِّنَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَهُدًى وَرَحْمَةٌ  ۚ فَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَصَدَفَ عَنْهَا ؕ سَنَجْزِى الَّذِيْنَ يَصْدِفُوْنَ عَنْ اٰيٰتِنَا سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَصْدِفُوْنَ‏(157)\nAW TAQOOLOO LAW ANNAA UNZELA A’LAYNAA KETAABO LAKUNNAA AHDAA MINHUM FAQAD JAAA-AKUM BAYNATUN MIN RABBEKUM WA HODANW WA RAHMAH FAMAN AZLAMO MIMMAN KAZZABA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WASADAFA A’NHAA SA-NAJZIL LAZEENA YASDEFOONA A’N AAYAATENAA SOOO-AL A’ZAABE BEMAA KAANOO YASDEFOONA.\nOr lest ye should say: “If the Book had only been sent down to us, we should have followed its guidance better than they.” Now then hath come unto you a clear (sign) from your Lord, and a guide and a mercy: then who could do more wrong than one who rejecteth Allah's signs, and turneth away therefrom? In good time shall We requite those who turn away from Our signs, with a dreadful penalty, for their turning away. \nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمُ الْمَلٰۤئِكَةُ اَوْ يَاْتِىَ رَبُّكَ اَوْ يَاْتِىَ بَعْضُ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّكَ ؕ يَوْمَ يَاْتِىْ بَعْضُ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّكَ لَا يَنْفَعُ نَفْسًا اِيْمَانُهَا لَمْ تَكُنْ اٰمَنَتْ مِنْ قَبْلُ اَوْ كَسَبَتْ فِىْۤ اِيْمَانِهَا خَيْرًا ؕ قُلِ انْتَظِرُوْۤا اِنَّا مُنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(158)\nHAL YANZOROONA ILLAA AN TAA-TEYAHOMUL AL-MALAAEKATU AW HATTAA RABBOKA AW HATTAA BA’ZUL AAYAATIL RABBEKA YAWMA YAATEE BA’ZUL AAYAATIL RABBEKA LAA YANFAU’N NAFSAN AEEMAANUHAA LAM TAKUN AAAMANAT MIN QABLO AW KASABAT FEE AEEMAANEHAA KHAYRAN QOLIL ANTAZEROOA INNAA MUNTAZEROONA.\nAre they waiting to see if the angels come to them, or thy Lord (Himself), or certain of the signs of thy Lord! the day that certain of the signs of thy Lord do come, no good will it do to a soul to believe in them then if it believed not before nor earned righteousness through its faith. Say: “Wait ye: we too are waiting.” \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ فَرَّقُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ وَكَانُوْا شِيَعًا لَّسْتَ مِنْهُمْ فِىْ شَىْءٍ ؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَمْرُهُمْ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(159)\nINNAL LAZEENA FARRAQOO DEENAHUM WA KAANOO AHLAHAA LLASTA MINHUM FEE SHAY-IN INNAMAA AAMRUHUM ELAL LAAHE SUMMA YUNABBEUHUM BEMAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nAs for those who divide their religion and break up into sects, thou hast no part in them in the least: their affair is with Allah: He will in the end tell them the truth of all that they did. \nمَنْ جَآءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهٗ عَشْرُ اَمْثَالِهَا ۚ وَمَنْ جَآءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَلَا يُجْزٰٓى اِلَّا مِثْلَهَا وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(160)\nMAN JAAA-A BIL-HASANATE FALAHU A’ASHRU AAMSAALEHAA WA MAN JAAA-A BIS-SAYYEATE FALAA YUJZAAA ILLAA MESLAHAA WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nHe that doeth good shall have ten times as much to his credit: He that doeth evil shall only be recompensed according to his evil: no wrong shall be done unto (any of) them. \nقُلْ اِنَّنِىْ هَدٰٮنِىْ رَبِّىْۤ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍۚ دِيْنًا قِيَمًا مِّلَّةَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ حَنِيْفًا ۚ وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(161)\nQUL INNANEE HADAANEAA RABBEE ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM DEENAN QEEMAN MMELLATA IBRAAHEEMA HANEEFAA WA MAA KAANA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nSay: “Verily, my Lord hath guided me to a way that is straight, a religion of right, the path (trod) by Abraham the true in Faith, and he (certainly) joined not gods with Allah.” \nقُلْ اِنَّ صَلَاتِىْ وَنُسُكِىْ وَ مَحْيَاىَ وَمَمَاتِىْ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(162)\nQUL INNAL SALAATEAA WANUSUKEAA WA MAHYAAAAA WAMAMAATEAA LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nSay: “Truly, my prayer and my service of sacrifice, my life and my death, are (all) for Allah, the Cherisher of the Worlds: \nلَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗۚ وَبِذٰلِكَ اُمِرْتُ وَاَنَا اَوَّلُ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(163)\nLAA SHAREEKA LAHU WABEZAALEKA AN A-A’BODA ANAT AAWLU AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nNo partner hath He: this am I commanded, and I am the first of those who bow to His will. \nقُلْ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَبْغِىْ رَبًّا وَّهُوَ رَبُّ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ ؕ وَلَا تَكْسِبُ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ اِلَّا عَلَيْهَاۚ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰى ۚ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ مَّرْجِعُكُمْ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ فِيْهِ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(164)\nQUL AAGHAYRA LAAHE AABGHEAA RABBAN WA RABBUL KULLE SHAY-IN WA LAA TAKSEBU KULLO NAFSIM ILLAA A’LAYHAA WA LAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM MMARJEU’UKUM FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM FEEHE TAKHTALEFOONA.\nSay: “Shall I seek for (my) Cherisher other than Allah, when He is the Cherisher of all things (that exist)? Every soul draws the meed of its acts on none but itself: no bearer of burdens can bear the burden of another. Your goal in the end is towards Allah: He will tell you the truth of the things wherein ye disputed.” \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَكُمْ خَلٰٓئِفَ الْاَرْضِ وَرَفَعَ بَعْضَكُمْ فَوْقَ بَعْضٍ دَرَجٰتٍ لِّيَبْلُوَكُمْ فِىْ مَاۤ اٰتٰٮكُمْؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ سَرِيْعُ الْعِقَابِ  ۖ وَاِنَّهٗ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(165)\nWA HOWA LAZEE JAA’ALAKUM KHALAAAEFA ARZE RA-FA-A’ BAA’ZAKUM FAWQA ELAA DARAJAATIN LLEEBLOOKUM FEE MAA AAATAAKUM INNAL RABBAKA SAREE-U’L E’QAAB WA INNAHU LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nIt is He Who hath made you (His) agents, inheritors of the earth: He hath raised you in ranks, some above others: that He may try you in the gifts He hath given you: for thy Lord is quick in punishment: yet He is indeed Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. ",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and contains a total of 165 verses. Imam Reza (a.s.) has said that this Surah was revealed accompanied by the descending of seventy thousand angels. These angels will ask forgiveness from Allah (s.w.t.) for any person who recites this Surah, and they will continue doing so until the Day of Judgement.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that if a person writes this Surah using musk or saffron and then drinks it (ie. puts the written Surah in water for its writing to dissolve) for six consecutive days, that person will be blessed abundantly and will be free from all problems and ailments. He will not loose his health or fall sick.\nThe 6th Holy Imam (a.s.) also said that this Surah must be accorded due respect as the name of Allah (s.w.t.) appears 70 times in it. If people knew the benefits of reciting this Surah, they would never leave it."
}
